\par\par \b \uc2 Rising sol: Peru's  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  at year-high after shaking off protest impact\b0\par\par\uc2 377 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Mai 2023\par 19:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 LIMA, May 11 (Reuters) - In a country shaken by years of political volatility, Peru's national \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has emerged as a mainstay of relative stability among Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, reaching its strongest level in a year this week.\par \par \uc2 After taking a hit during the nearly two-year presidency of Pedro Castillo, the Peruvian sol is bouncing back just months after his removal and subsequent protests that briefly stifled the economy of the world's second largest copper producer.\par \par \uc2 For the third straight day Thursday, the sol had its best showing since May 2022, trading at 3.665 soles per dollar, data from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and traders showed.\par \par \uc2 Latin America's main \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have strengthened sharply in recent months, like Mexico's peso, which hit a five-year high this week.\par \par \uc2 Peru's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , however, has not deviated much in value since 2000 and it is up some 3% so far in 2023 from its closing price at the end of December.\par \par \uc2 "Since the beginning of the century, we have depreciated something like 6% (...) while other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have depreciated by 50%, 100% or 150%," the head of \uc2 Peru's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Julio Velarde said Wednesday at an event launching a commemorative coin.\par \par \uc2 In this context, "the sol is one of the most stable \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the region among large and medium-sized countries," Velarde said.\par \par \uc2 Of Peru's ten presidents this century, most have respected free market policies with rigid fiscal discipline. This allowed the economy to enjoy record growth rates for years, accumulate large net reserves and have a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market that moves freely with supply and demand.\par \par \uc2 In this context, \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has only \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market by buying or selling dollars or financial instruments to mitigate the sol's volatility.\par \par \uc2 "What has been shown in 20 or 30 years is that the sol is a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  that guarantees value recovery, which is why Peru has more or less 40% of its debt in soles," Economy Minister Alex Contreras said at a recent event.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Marco Aquino; Additional reporting by Hernan Nessi in Buenos Aires Editing by Alistair Bell) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2023-5-11T18:56:36.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020230511ej5b03vw5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
