\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Peruvian sol closes 2022 as one of the strongest  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  in the region, why is this?\b0\par\par\uc2 1,228 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Dezember 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 On the eve of entering a new year, it is important to highlight the performance of the Peruvian sol during 2022. In a scenario of high volatility for the economy due to international shocks and the country's internal collateral effects, our \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has consolidated itself as one of the strongest and most stable in Latin America.\par \par \uc2 According to the \uc2 Central Reserve Bank of Peru\uc2  (\uc2 BCR\uc2 ), the US dollar closed this year 2022 slightly down at S/ 3.8070, registering a depreciation of 4.61% compared to the close of 2021 when it was quoted at S/ 3.991.\par \par \uc2 In view of this result, the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has positioned itself in a favorable position compared to the Chilean or Colombian peso. According to \uc2 Bloomberg\uc2 's ranking on the performance of the main Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar, the Peruvian sol occupies a solid fourth position, surpassed only by the Uruguayan peso, the Brazilian real and the Mexican peso.\par \par \uc2 According to analysts, the Peruvian sol remains one of the most attractive \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the region due to the solid political and fiscal position of the country's economy, despite still high interest rates. It is also driven by its strong ties with its main trading partners, the United States and China.\par \par \uc2 Volatile exchange rate\par \par \uc2 Despite market volatility, Omar Aza\u241\'00\'F1edo, an economist at the Universidad del Pac\u237\'00\'EDfico, told Infobae that the Peruvian sol remains one of the strongest in the region against the dollar, having appreciated between 4% and 5% during 2022.\par \par \uc2 You may be interested in: Dollar in Peru: Its price closes lower at S/ 3.80 on New Year's Eve\par \par \uc2 "The greenback during this year has registered high volatility, but this has not only happened in Peru but also in the whole world. However, the \uc2 Central Reserve Bank of Peru\uc2  (\uc2 BCR\uc2 ) has done an outstanding job in its monetary policy to prevent the dollar from continuing to rise," the expert pointed out.\par \par \uc2 Thus, the exchange rate in Peru reached a maximum level of S/ 4.00 at the end of October and a minimum of S/ 3.63 at the beginning of April 2022. However, analysts for 2023 expect a high dollar fluctuating between S/ 3.85 to S/ 3.95 due to the international scenario.\par \par \uc2 "The \uc2 BCR\uc2  has had a fairly good management of the monetary policy, but it is not enough, since in these times of global crisis is where more growth, investment, welfare and confidence should be generated, which is lacking in the country", emphasized Aza\u241\'00\'F1edo.\par \par \uc2 For his part, Diego Macera, general manager of the Peruvian Institute of Economics (IPE), stated that the good performance of the exchange rate in the country is due to the fact that it has a strong inertial component that provides certain expectations to the market. "We have the most stable exchange rate in the region in the last 20 years," he added.\par \par \uc2 BCR \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the president of the Central Reserve Bank (\uc2 BCR\uc2 ), Julio Velarde, pointed out that, so far, in a context of social protests and political uncertainty, no major effect on the country's exchange market has been noticed.\par \par \uc2 "What has affected little is the exchange rate, and I think the perception has been that this is going to end, that is, it is a temporary thing, and in which case there would be no reason to be betting heavily against the sun. So far, no major effect has been noticed", explained the official during the presentation of the latest Inflation Report.\par \par \uc2 You may be interested in: Dollar in Peru: How the political crisis impacts the exchange rate\par \par \uc2 During 2022, Julio Velarde indicated that the \uc2 BCR\uc2  has made a net sale of USD 1,234 million in the exchange market. "The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has had a quite small \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year, the exchange pressures have not occurred. In fact, the sol has been appreciating, without major \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \uc2 BCR\uc2 ", he said.\par \par \uc2 The president of the \uc2 BCR\uc2  referred that some \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the region appreciated during 2022, in a context of rising interest rates, considering, in addition, that the dollar reached its highest value in 20 years.\par \par \uc2 "The few \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the world that are appreciating, which can be counted on the fingers of one hand, are those of Peru, Mexico, Brazil and Russia. These \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have been strengthened this year, in a scenario where the dollar has been strong globally," Velarde noted.\par \par \uc2 Outlook for 2023\par \par \uc2 The Peruvian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will show some weakness in 2023, in an environment of greater global risk perception and a decrease in the interest rate differential between soles and dollars, which will reduce the appetite for emerging economies' assets.\par \par \uc2 In this sense, \uc2 BBVA Research\uc2  projects that the exchange rate will end between S/ 4.00 and S/ 4.10 per dollar in 2023. "For the following months, we anticipate that the exchange rate dynamics will be more linked to external factors (monetary adjustment of the FED and lower appetite for risk will induce capital outflows from emerging economies)," the bank indicated.\par \par \uc2 You may be interested in: Dollar in Peru: How much could the exchange rate be worth for the New Year?\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Credicorp Capital anticipates that the exchange rate in 2023 would remain relatively stable, to end at S/ 3.85. However, Scotiabank estimates that the dollar could reach a higher value between S/ 3.85 to S/ 3.95.\par \par \uc2 "The country's exchange rate is well supported by the level of trade surplus, which is between USD 11 billion to USD 12 billion so far this year, as well as its high level of international reserves," said Mario Guerrero, assistant manager of Economics at Scotiabank's Economic Research Department.\par \par \uc2 Likewise, the expert affirmed that, in the context of a stronger dollar, the effects of the war between Russia and Ukraine, among other factors, could boost a higher U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  that could reach a higher value at the beginning of 2023.\par \par \uc2 You may be interested in: What to expect for the Peruvian economy next year?\par \par \uc2 "When the dollar price approaches S/4 there is discomfort from the \uc2 BCR\uc2  because it increases the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  pattern. \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2  is working with a lateral pattern in the face of the international scenario", said the analyst.\par \par \uc2 Dollar still high in Peru\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, Aza\u241\'00\'F1edo pointed out that an average exchange rate of S/ 3.90 is high and a crisis scenario, since as we remember before the pandemic the dollar was quoted at S/ 3.30 or S/ 3.20.\par \par \uc2 Likewise, he said that it is complicated to see again an exchange rate falling back to S/ 3.50 in the next months. "For the exchange rate to reach that quotation, it is not feasible at this moment, but it could happen if many things change in the international and local context", he added.\par \par \uc2 However, he considered that the local context is worrisome, since if it worsens it could give a negative signal, which could push the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  further up, close to S/ 3.90.\par \par \uc2 Outlook and challenges facing the Peruvian economy in 2023\par \par \uc2 Crisis in Peru and an economy that has been on a tightrope through 2022\par \par \uc2 Alex Contreras: "This year poverty will probably not be reduced in Peru".\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020230101eicv0004g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
