\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 What does the one dollar bill that can be worth US$ 150,000 look like to collectors?\b0\par\par\uc2 2,577 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 November 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Numismatics is a passion that has united thousands of people, so it is not surprising that collectors are willing to pay exorbitant sums of money for a banknote that has defects or anomalies, since some have a great monetary value due to certain curious characteristics.\par \par \uc2 An example of this is the 2014 one dollar bill, which for having a simple printing error, can currently be worth up to US$ 150,000. Find out, below, how this flaw was generated and how you can identify it.\par \par \uc2 One-dollar bills worth up to US$ 150,000In 2014, the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2 , the government agency in charge of printing U.S. dollars, mistakenly issued two equal runs of 6.4 million one-dollar bills.\par \par \uc2 That same year, the first batch of dollars with error was distributed in the state of New York and, curiously, two years later another group exactly the same arrived in Washington.\par \par \uc2 This mistake caused 6.4 million "even bills" of one dollar with the same serial number to be distributed around the world, although only 9 of these pairs have been found so far. Due to their rarity and the difficulty in finding them, some collectors are offering up to US$ 150,000 for them.\par \par \uc2 How to identify these one dollar bills?To know if your dollar bill is worth thousands of dollars, you should check its serial number, which should be between B00000001 and B00250000 or B03200001 and B09600000.\par \par \uc2 In addition to this feature you should make sure that the bill has a \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  stamp with the letter "B" on it. Also, the serial number should end with a star.\par \par \uc2 What do the one dollar bills sold for US$200 look like?The Federal Reserve of the United States issued in 1969 a series of one dollar bills, which have an error in the "Gutter note", reason why there are many collectors willing to pay a fortune for them.\par \par \uc2 One of these bills sells for US$ 200 (approximately S/. 783) on \uc2 eBay\uc2 . However, it is worth clarifying that in order to know how much money would be paid for them, it is necessary to consult an interested buyer, although they are sold at that price on the aforementioned website.\par \par \uc2 Ladder dollar billsLadder dollar bills are the rarest in history. This is formed in the serial number of the bill and bears the numbers one through eight in ascending or descending order (12345678 or 87654321). Because it is very difficult to find its value in the collector's market is around US$ 5,000.\par \par \uc2 Variations of the ladder pattern include numbers in order that do not start with one, such as 00123456 or 034567. These can also be in reverse order; however, both variations are more common on one dollar bills and less valuable than the authentic ones.\par \par \uc2 What are the dollar denominations that exist?The \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve Board\uc2  currently issues seven denominations of dollar bills. These are:\par \par \uc2 US$ 1 billUS$ 2 billUS$ 5 billUS$ 10 billUS$ 20 billUS$ 50 billUS$ 100 bill.How many US$ 1 dollar bills worth up to US$ 150,000 have been sold today?So far, only nine pairs of one-dollar bills have been found that were duplicated by errors, which means there are millions of these circulating in the United States and around the world. To confirm that you have a bill of this denomination and that it belongs to the group of the most sought after by buyers, you should consult with a specialist.\par \par \uc2 When did the first one dollar bill appear?The history of U.S. banknotes is one of the main aspects that determine the value of dollars. Therefore, it is necessary to have a certain amount of knowledge on the subject. For example, the first one dollar bill was printed on May 10, 1775, during the colonial period. This happened during the American Revolutionary War, so there were many obstacles in the process of printing the bill.\par \par \uc2 How do you know if a dollar is real or counterfeit?Just as a dollar can cost an exorbitant amount of money, there is also the possibility that it is counterfeit. Below, we share some tips to identify if a dollar is counterfeit:\par \par \uc2 Dollars have high image quality, so you should check if yours has a clear design.The numbers on dollars are sharper, so you will be able to tell if it is a fake or not by the resolution of the digits.Real dollars have amber tones in their presentation, while counterfeit dollars have light colors.Counterfeit dollars have a tendency to be rougher.If you hold a real dollar up against the light, you will notice the watermark with Benjamin Franklin's image. On the other hand, on counterfeit dollars, the watermark can be seen with the naked eye and has an almost yellowish hue.The edges of the real dollars are sharp, while the fake ones are usually blurred.Who was George Washington, the character that appears on the dollar bill?Since 1869, George Washington, who is considered the Father of the Nation and was also the first president of the United States, has appeared on the lowest denomination bill.\par \par \uc2 Who are the characters that appear on the dollar bills?The characters that appear on the different denominations of dollar bills are:\par \par \uc2 US$ 1 bill: George WashingtonUS$ 2 bill: Thomas JeffersonUS$ 5 bill: Abraham Lincoln10 US$ bill: Alexander Hamilton20 US Dollar Bill: Andrew Jackson50 US Dollar Bill: Ulysses S. GrantUS$ 100 bill: Benjamin Franklin.What is the mystery of the two-dollar bill?The US$ 2 bill features the image of Thomas Jefferson, plus a vignette depicting the signing of the U.S. Declaration of Independence. Its mystery lies in the fact that due to its lack of use, this bill was discontinued in 1966 until it was reissued in 1976 for the bicentennial of the American Revolution.\par \par \uc2 How do you know if a US$ 2 bill is real?The paper of the two dollar bill will allow a person to tell if it is real or counterfeit. When handled, the bill should have a crisp sound, as it is made of one-quarter linen and three-quarters cotton.\par \par \uc2 Why do we use the dollar as an international \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ?In recent years, according to Diego Marrero on the AFP Habitat website, 61% of the world's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves are in US dollars. The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is used for 60% of world trade.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar is one of the world's main \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , along with the euro, the pound, the yen and the renminbi, and is included in the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2 's basket of Special Drawing Rights \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . How did its importance come about?\par \par \uc2 It all goes back to the end of World War II, when the United States became the major hegemonic superpower. Before the end of the war, the \uc2 Bretton Woods\uc2  agreement (the United Nations monetary and financial settlement in 1944) established an international monetary system where the dollar became the main reference \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for trade around the world.\par \par \uc2 What is the dollar made of?Interestingly, a dollar bill is not made of paper. The formula to make them stronger involves a composition of cotton and linen.\par \par \uc2 Why is it called a dollar?In the 16th century, coins were minted in St. Joachimsthal, a town in Bohemia, as the place was considered to have the purest silver in the world. Thus, the coins were christened Joachmisthaler, from which the popular name Thaler was derived.\par \par \uc2 Gradually, some regions of Europe began to call the coins Daler. In addition, this was the name Spain used as the official \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the American colonies. Until, finally, with the independence of the United States, came the issuance of coins and bills in 1985, so Congress decided to call these as dollar and dollars.\par \par \uc2 What does it mean to be given a dollar?As a kind of tradition, carrying a dollar in your wallet or purse is a sign of good fortune and wealth, so it is usually given or received as a gift a specific dollar bill.\par \par \uc2 Where can I buy cheap dollars in Peru?Although the exchange rate of dollars to soles is constantly changing, the truth is that more and more people are in the need to acquire these bills, either for purchases abroad, etc.. The following is a list of places where you can buy dollars in Peru:\par \par \uc2 BanksExchange housesShopping mallsAirportsStreet money changers.What does US$ mean in money?Abbreviations such as US$ or USD mean that they refer to the U.S. dollar, thus the legal \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the United States.\par \par \uc2 How much is US$ 1 in S/ 1?The exchange rate from dollar to soles varies daily; however, today, the value of $1 converted S/ 1 appears within the values of S/ 3,890 the purchase and S/ 3,930 the sale in the parallel market, according to the website cuantoestaeldolar.pe.\par \par \uc2 Where is it advisable to exchange dollars in Lima?In Lima there are many places where you can exchange dollars. For this reason we leave you some options so that the exchange of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is favorable and safe for you.\par \par \uc2 The airport or terminalThe hotel where you are stayingFinancial institutionsExchange housesMoney changers in the street.What is the blue dollar and the official dollar?The blue dollar is the bill that is bought outside the formal circuit, mainly known as parallel dollar or informal dollar. It receives this name in Argentina and other regions. On the other hand, the official dollar is the one issued by banking entities.\par \par \uc2 Why is the price of the dollar important?The dollar is important because its market value has a direct impact on the global economy and politics, as well as on the fundamental decisions of governments, investors and businessmen, so it is also part of the public interest.\par \par \uc2 How many years does a dollar last?Approximately, a dollar bill lasts between 6 to 7 years. These are the years of life of each bill today, according to the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Education Program (CEP) website:\par \par \uc2 US$ 1 bill: 6 to 7 years.US$ 5 bill: 4 yearsUS$ 10 bill: 5 yearsUS$ 20 bill: 7 yearsUS$ 50 bill: 12 yearsUS$ 100 bill: 22 years.Other dollar bills that were issuedAlthough the best known are the US$ 1, US$ 50 and US$ 100 bills, the truth is that in the past 3, 5, 10, 25 and 50 cent bills were also issued under the context of the American Civil War or Civil War in the 1860s, according to a report by the Midpoint website.\par \par \uc2 What's the phrase on the dollar?Since 1956, all dollar bills have had the phrase "In God we trust", translated into Spanish as "Confiamos en Dios" (We trust in God). This is because President \uc2 Dwight D. Eisenhower\uc2  enacted a bill in which U.S. coins would have the phrase inscribed on them, so Congress ordered it to be added to the bills as well.\par \par \uc2 What is the Canadian dollar?The Canadian dollar is the official \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  used in Canada. It was introduced in July 1858 and is symbolized by C$ or CAD.\par \par \uc2 U.S. dollar or Canadian dollar?Although both \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have the denomination "dollar", in terms of exchange rate, it is the U.S. dollar that has a higher monetary value. This is because it is considered a strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , for economic and financial reasons.\par \par \uc2 How much is a Canadian dollar worth?At the exchange rate, the Canadian dollar is worth between 3.04 soles and 3.30 soles.\par \par \uc2 What other countries use the U.S. dollar as their official \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ?The United States is not the only country that uses the U.S. dollar as its official \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Here are the other nations that use U.S. coins and bills.\par \par \uc2 EcuadorEl SalvadorMarshall IslandsZimbabweEast TimorMicronesiaPalau.What is the largest dollar bill?Between 1934 and 1935, during the Great Depression, the U.S. Treasurer printed 42,000 of the US$100,000 bills. This was the largest denomination piece of paper money ever produced by the US.\par \par \uc2 Finding such a specimen is really difficult so counterfeits are relatively common. However, a handful of real US$100,000 bills, including an uncut sheet of 12 sample bills, are on display at the \uc2 Federal Reserve Bank of San Francisco\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Who is on the $100,000 dollar?The bill is imprinted with the image of Woodrow Wilson, the 28th president of the United States, who took office from 1913 to 1921. It should be noted that this bill was only used for internal transactions between the Federal Reserve Banks.\par \par \uc2 The dollar bill that sells for US$ 95,000 dollarsIn 1977, the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2  issued a series of one-dollar bills, which although not in circulation, have a high value in the collectors' market: US$ 95,000. The reason for their high price is due to the fact that these issues have a misalignment error and are considered "rare".\par \par \uc2 How does the increase in the price of the dollar affect them?The increase in the price of the dollar generates an increase in the cost of credit, not only in the United States, but also worldwide. In other words, borrowing money has become more expensive for countries, companies and individuals. As a result, activity slows down and recovery becomes more difficult.\par \par \uc2 Who determines the price of the dollar?First, the price of the dollar is determined by the free market. This means two things: when there is a shortage of dollars, the exchange rate goes up; conversely, in times of dollar abundance, it goes down. Secondly, the Central Reserve Bank (BCR), the entity in charge of exchange rate policy in \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to avoid abrupt fluctuations in the price of the dollar.\par \par \uc2 What is the most expensive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the world?The most expensive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the world is the Kuwaiti dinar (KWD). Kuwait has the sixth largest oil reserves in the world, making it one of the richest Arab countries on the Asian continent. Currently its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is the most expensive and valued \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . One Kuwaiti dinar is equivalent to US$ 3.30.\par \par \uc2 What is the cheapest \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the world?The most devalued \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is the Venezuelan Sovereign Bolivar (VES), which, after the crisis suffered in Venezuela, was devalued to the point of exchanging 1 dollar for 1,552,540 VES.\par \par \uc2 How many intis were equivalent to one dollar?The number of zeros was a main characteristic of the Peruvian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 1990. Thus, one dollar was worth 300,000 intis.\par \par \uc2 How long did the Intis circulate?In May 1985 the first coins expressed in intis were put into circulation, while the first banknotes were put into circulation in December of the same year. The inti was valid as a monetary unit until June 30, 1991 (6 years).\par \par \uc2 Why are there 1 sol coins painted red?The phenomenon of coins painted red follows a common line: they are only those that have the design prior to the one incorporated in 2012 (the one that does not have the denomination in number). When in doubt, Abraham de la Melena Ruiz, specialist in Circulating \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Analysis of the \uc2 Central Reserve Bank of Peru\uc2  (BCRP), explained where these red spots came from.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020221114eibe0083x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
