\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Price of the dollar in Peru LIVE: The exchange rate falls again and closes at S/3.97 this Thursday\b0\par\par\uc2 1,149 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Oktober 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Credicorp Capital: dollar rise responds to higher interest rates in the world\par \par \uc2 The price of the dollar has been rising in the world as a safe haven \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the face of global uncertainty and the rise in interest rates in the United States has caused this trend to be further enhanced, said the general manager of Credicorp Capital SAF, Rocio Coloma.\par \par \uc2 "The dollar has several components. This \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the world has been rising as a safe haven \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the high interest rates have caused the dollar to strengthen even more", commented the specialist.\par \par \uc2 In addition to this, in the local scenario, political instability also has an impact on the search for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , she said. In this sense, the price of the dollar in the country would close the year above four soles, projected the Credicorp Capital SAF executive.\par \par \uc2 This is how the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been performing this year\par \par \uc2 So far in 2022, as of October 24, the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciated 0.28%, taking into account that the price of the dollar closed last Monday at S/ 4.002, after having ended 2021 at S/ 3.991.\par \par \uc2 So far this year, as of October 21, the Central Reserve Bank (\uc2 BCR\uc2 ) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly in the market selling US$ 1,226 million, according to figures from the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 It is worth mentioning that the price of the dollar dropped 0.18% at the end of the third quarter of this year, since it ended September 30 at 3.984 soles, according to \uc2 BCR\uc2  data.\par \par \uc2 The quotation of the US \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  advanced 3.35% in September 2022 with respect to the previous month, after having ended last August 31 at 3.855 soles.\par \par \uc2 Analysts at FocusEconomics Consensus Forecast LatinFocus, in their October 2022 report, forecast that the dollar would be at 3.95 soles at the end of the year.\par \par \uc2 Price of the dollar in Peru fell again and closed at S/ 3.97 on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, October 27, the price of the U.S. dollar closed down again at S/ 3.9760, registering a 0.33% drop compared to Wednesday's closing price of S/ 3.9890, according to the \uc2 Central Reserve Bank of Peru\uc2  (BCRP).\par \par \uc2 So far in 2022, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  accumulates a 0.38% retreat compared to the last quote of 2021, at S/ 3.991.\par \par \uc2 In the morning, the exchange rate in the parallel market was quoted at S/ 3.965 for buying and S/ 3.990 for selling. Meanwhile, at the main banks' windows it reached S/ 4.0060.\par \par \uc2 According to \uc2 Bloomberg\uc2 's ranking of the main Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , during this year, the Peruvian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar, despite having registered two consecutive days exceeding the barrier of S/ 4.00, still continues to appreciate by 0.3%, surpassed by the Mexican peso with 2.9%, the Brazilian real with 3.6%, the Uruguayan peso with 9.2%. While the Chilean peso recorded a depreciation of -10.4% and the Colombian peso -16.5%.\par \par \uc2 What to do in the face of the strengthening of the dollar?\par \par \uc2 According to Washington Lopez, CEO of Washington Capital, the strengthening of the dollar occurs due to external and macroeconomic factors, such as the contractionary monetary policy of the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  in the United States, which seeks to counteract the blows of inflation not seen in the last 40 years.\par \par \uc2 As a result, \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the euro, the pound sterling and the yen have also recorded historic lows. And this strengthening of the dollar affects Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which is why, this year alone, in May it was recorded at S/3.60, and now in October it reached S/4.00, with a perspective of being above this level in the coming months.\par \par \uc2 "It is important to warn, from now on, that the situation may worsen, our estimate is that the dollar will exceed the barrier of S/ 4.15 or even S/ 4.30, that is why, Peruvians are still in time to dollarize their surpluses or capital so as not to be affected by this depreciation of the exchange rate," said Lopez.\par \par \uc2 He added that this should be a medium-term view, for people who seek to dollarize their surpluses and not change them to soles in a long time because, if they return to the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a year, they would be making a loss in case they need to make use of these soles.\par \par \uc2 Today's BCR \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 At 11:05 a.m.: A S/ 200 million 3-month swap for sale (fixed rate) was placed, at an average rate of 3.71 percent.\par \par \uc2 At 10:20 am: The following auction was called: Swap Exchange Sale (fixed rate) for 3 months for S/ 200 million.\par \par \uc2 At 09:50 a.m.: S/ 300 million 3-month Swap Exchange Sale (fixed rate) at an average rate of 3.75 percent was placed.\par \par \uc2 At 09:20 am: The Central Reserve Bank (\uc2 BCR\uc2 ) called for the following auction: Swap Exchange Sale (fixed rate) for 3 months for S/ 300 million.\par \par \uc2 The dollar opened slightly lower at the beginning of the session on Thursday, October 27th.\par \par \uc2 The price of the US dollar in Peru opened this Thursday, October 27 with a slight decline, after \uc2 Standard & Poor's\uc2  (S&P) ratified the country's credit rating and maintained it in stable outlook.\par \par \uc2 The exchange rate trades at S/ 3.9846 per dollar, registering a 0.11% drop compared to Wednesday's closing price of S/ 3.9890, according to Bloomberg.\par \par \uc2 This morning, the price of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the parallel market or exchange houses is S/ 3.995, while at the main banks' windows it is quoted at S/ 4.08.\par \par \uc2 It is worth noting that today's slight drop comes after recent U.S. economic data reinforced speculations that the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  will slow down its interest rate hike.\par \par \uc2 /america/peru/2022/10/26/price-of-the-dollar-in-peru-held-at-s-4-for-second-consecutive-day-that-is-due/\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, the Peruvian dollar remained at S/. 4.00 for the second consecutive day.\par \par \uc2 The price of the US dollar in Peru closed this Tuesday for the second consecutive day at S/ 4.00 despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the \uc2 Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BCRP).\par \par \uc2 According to the monetary entity, the greenback closed its quotation with a slight decline against the sol in the exchange session of this Tuesday, October 25 and reached S/ 4.000.\par \par \uc2 Thus, it depreciated -0.05% compared to Monday's closing price of S/ 4.0020, reaching its highest level since December 24 last year, in a context of global strengthening of the American \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020221027eiar00fsc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
