\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Dollar closes at S/ 3.98, despite \uc2 BCR \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 352 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Oktober 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The price of the dollar in \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2  closed higher on Thursday, amid a significant advance of the greenback in global markets due to renewed fears of aggressive interest rate hikes in the United States, supported by statements from various \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  (Fed) officials.\par \par \uc2 The exchange rate ended at S/ 3.981 per dollar, up 0.28% against Wednesday's close at S/ 3.970, according to the Peruvian Central Reserve Bank (\uc2 BCR\uc2 ).\par \par \uc2 So far this year, the greenback accumulates a decline of 0.25% compared to the last quotation of 2021 at S/ 3.991.\par \par \uc2 Today, US$ 311 million were traded in the market at an average price of S/ 3.9831, indicated Allisson Perez, \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at Renta4 SAB.\par \par \uc2 "During the day, the demand came from offshores and corporates, while the supply was from the \uc2 BCR\uc2 , which \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  with \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps for S/ 600 million for six months at an average rate of 3.98%\u8243\'20\'33, he said.\par \par \uc2 He added that during the day the dollar reached a maximum level of S/ 3.9890 and a minimum level of S/ 3.9750. This Thursday there were maturities of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps for S/ 900 million.\par \par \uc2 In the parallel market or the main exchange houses the dollar is bought at S/ 3.960 and sold at S/ 3.966, according to data from the portal cuantoestaeldolar.pe.\par \par \uc2 Today is the meeting of the \uc2 Central Reserve Bank of Peru\uc2  (\uc2 BCR\uc2 ), which will know if it will raise the reference interest rate by 25 basis points, which would reach 7%.\par \par \uc2 Globally, there is negative data in the United States, due to new unemployment claims, which means that there are more people unemployed than expected. Despite this, investors continue to take refuge in the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if markets stopped functioning properly, said \uc2 San Francisco Fed\uc2  President \uc2 Mary Daly\uc2 , who added that the current situation does not justify such a move and that the Fed maintains its plan to curb inflation with further rate hikes.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020221006eia600aiy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
