\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 The dollar continues to rise: it closed yesterday at S/3.950 and these are the factors that appreciate the  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 570 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 September 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The price of the dollar in Peru closed Tuesday higher and traded at S/3.950. This is an advance of 0.22% of its value compared to Monday's close, at S/3.941 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 Hugo Perea, chief economist at \uc2 BBVA Research\uc2  in Peru, indicated that this was due to the global strengthening of the dollar after the United States suggested that it could continue to raise its interest rates.\par \par \uc2 "It was not so much the decision to raise the rate, the surprise came when the macroeconomic projections that the participants of the Federal Open Market \b \highlight22\uc2 Operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  Committee of the United States, who decide what they will do with monetary policy rates, were released. There they hinted that they are going to raise rates more than the government expected", he said.\par \par \uc2 This situation occurred after last week the \uc2 US Federal Reserve\uc2  raised the interest rate by 75 basis points.\par \par \uc2 "If the U.S. raises its rates too much there could be a recession. When there are uncertainties and fears, investors look for refuge \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , they release positions in emerging markets such as Peru, Chile, Colombia and that pressures the exchange rate and depreciates the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ", he explained.\par \par \uc2 Perea pointed out that during Monday the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the region closed with an average depreciation of 2% and that the impact was lower in \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2  due to the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the Central Reserve Bank, which placed S/824 million of exchange swaps for sale at nine months with an average rate of 3.85%.\par \par \uc2 According to Gianina Villavicencio, \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  Brokerage Manager at Renta4 SAB Peru, the US \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue to appreciate this week.\par \par \uc2 "[Yesterday] the highest peak was at S/3.95. This week it could reach S/3.98\u8243\'20\'33, he indicated.\par \par \uc2 IN ECONOMY : Construction sector projects a 0.9% drop this 2022\par \par \uc2 He also added that the United States will maintain the monetary policy regarding the increase in rates, so the upward trend of the dollar price would remain, at least, for the rest of the year.\par \par \uc2 The pound sterling\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, the pound sterling plummeted to a record low on Monday as the \uc2 British government\uc2  announced a bold tax cut valued at 45 billion pounds. Yesterday it traded at US$1.0327 to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 "In the UK we are seeing rates that are going to keep rising, inflation that keeps rising, a depreciating and volatile economy versus oil and hydrocarbon prices, plus a tax package that would generate more damage than growth could [mitigate]," explained Cesar Romero, head of research at Renta4 SAB.\par \par \uc2 "UK enacted a significant tax cut to try to stimulate the economy. This has been perceived as a risk that it may increase inflation," Perea noted in the same vein.\par \par \uc2 During the day, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of England indicated that it "will not hesitate" to change interest rates to control inflation and stabilize the pound. However, the government's measures would not mitigate the effects.\par \par \uc2 "It is an economy whose debt to GDP is already over 100%, with an investment package that includes a tax cut for banks and high net worth individuals, so that creates quite a bit of anxiety. This would lead to a 200-point increase in rates that year," said Romero.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220929ei9s001li\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
