\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Dollar closes with a very strong rise of S/ 3.76 despite \uc2 BCR \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 495 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Juni 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The price of the dollar in \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2  closed sharply higher today, amid market and investor concerns about a possible further slowdown of the global economy that could enter recession.\par \par \uc2 The exchange rate trades at S/ 3.763 per dollar, an advance of 0.91% against Wednesday's close at S/ 3.729, according to data from the \uc2 Central Reserve Bank of Peru\uc2  (\uc2 BCR\uc2 ).\par \par \uc2 So far this year, the greenback accumulates a 5.71% decline compared to the last quotation of 2021 at S/ 3.991.\par \par \uc2 In the local market, US$ 280 million were traded at an average price of S/ 3.7534. The demand came mainly from corporate investors and from S/ 385 million of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps maturities.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 BCR\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  by placing \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps for S/ 700 million and sold US$ 50 million at an average exchange rate of S/ 3.766.\par \par \uc2 "The dollar gained positions and was trading at 104.02 at the close of the market due to growing concerns about a possible recession in the US on the second day of Fed Chairman \uc2 Jerome Powell\uc2 's appearance," said Asvim Asencios, \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at Renta4 SAB.\par \par \uc2 "Copper reached minimum prices and this increased concerns about the evolution of the local economy in the face of a possible lower demand for metals and commodities in which we are the main exporters," he added.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, in the parallel market or the main exchange houses, the dollar is bought at S/ 3.720 and sold at S/ 3.760, according to the portal cuantoestaeldolar.pe.\par \par \uc2 Regionally, most Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and stock exchanges were trading with losses on Thursday, amid market and investor concerns about a possible further slowdown of the global economy that could enter recession.\par \par \uc2 "Continued interest rate hikes to curb inflation have put an additional drag on the economy's recovery, and there is already open talk about the possibility of a global recession, which increases market nervousness," said a trader.\par \par \uc2 According to Reuters, the day before, the president of the \uc2 United States Federal Reserve\uc2  (Fed), \uc2 Jerome Powell\uc2 , indicated that the entity is fully committed to controlling prices, even if doing so would risk facing an economic recession.\par \par \uc2 "We are not trying to cause, and I don't think we need to cause, a recession," Powell assured a hearing before the Senate Banking Committee, although he acknowledged that recession was "certainly a possibility" and the events of recent months in the world have made it more difficult to reduce inflation without causing a drop in activity.\par \par \uc2 "It is essential that we reduce inflation if we are to have a sustained period of strong labor market conditions that benefit everyone," Powell said. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be looking in the coming months for "compelling evidence" of a slowdown in price pressures before tapering the interest rate increases initiated three months ago.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220623ei6n00es9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
