\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Dollar closed at S/ 3.741 on higher risk appetite in global markets\b0\par\par\uc2 400 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Februar 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The price of the dollar in Peru closed higher on Wednesday, despite increased risk appetite and after an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \uc2 Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2  (\uc2 BCR\uc2 ).\par \par \uc2 The exchange rate ended the session at S/ 3.741, an advance of 0.28% against Tuesday's close, at S/ 3.730, according to data from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 So far this year, the greenback accumulates a 6.26% decline compared to the last quotation of 2021, at S/ 3.991.\par \par \uc2 "Locally, US$ 324 million were traded at an average price of S/ 3.7162, the \uc2 BCR\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  with direct sales for US$ 1 million at an exchange rate of 3.7500\u8243\'20\'33, indicated Allisson Perez, \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at Renta4 SAB.\par \par \uc2 "During the morning, the dollar opened lower, as there was a strong supply of dollars from non-residents, which caused the dollar price to reach its lowest level of the day at an exchange rate of S/ 3.6680. After that, the exchange rate reversed due to corporate demand", he added.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, in the parallel market or the main exchange houses, the dollar was bought at S/ 3.715 and sold at S/ 3.755, according to the portal cuantoestaeldolar.pe.\par \par \uc2 At regional level, most Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and stock exchanges registered gains on Wednesday, boosted by the dollar's retreat and a greater appetite for risk assets, as expectations of a possible armed conflict between Russia and Ukraine diminished, despite the fact that the situation continues to be tense.\par \par \uc2 According to Reuters, the euro rose against the dollar on Wednesday, as investors braced for developments in the Ukrainian crisis after Western countries announced sanctions against Russia for sending troops to separatist regions.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Russian President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  said Wednesday that Russia is always open to diplomacy but puts its own national security interests first and will continue to strengthen its military in the face of a "difficult international situation."\par \par \uc2 "Internationally, there is still tension in the markets, as Ukraine has declared a state of emergency, which they indicate may last more than 30 days, due to its ongoing conflict with Russia, as they maintain a military presence on Ukraine's borders. Consequently, the Ukrainian parliament authorized the use of weapons so that they can act in self-defense", said Perez.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220223ei2n00b1c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
