\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 3-Peruvian markets retreat as President Castillo seeks new cabinet\b0\par\par\uc2 499 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Februar 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 (Adds market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  detail, Citi commentary)\par \par \uc2 LIMA, Feb 1 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the Lima stock market fell on Tuesday amid uncertainty as President Pedro Castillo sought to form a new cabinet following the resignation of his prime minister, in a new crisis for his government.\par \par \uc2 Peru's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the sol , closed the day down 1.01% at 3.8810/3.8850 soles to the dollar, in the steepest daily decline since July 30, 2021, two days after President Castillo took office.\par \par \uc2 The sol's decline occurred despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  placing some 1.1 billion soles in certificates of deposit and exchange swap, in an attempt to halt the depreciation.\par \par \uc2 The sol had been gaining ground since December and in the whole of January it rose 3.63%. Meanwhile, the Lima stock exchange benchmark yielded 1.0%, according to traders and market data.\par \par \uc2 "This base we had of 'no news, good news' was broken this week," a trader who asked not to be identified told Reuters.\par \par \uc2 Castillo, a rural school teacher who surprisingly won last year's presidential election, i announced on Monday that he decided to change his prime minister Mirtha Vasquez and reshuffle the cabinet, in what will be his third government team in just over half a year in office.\par \par \uc2 The now former head of the cabinet of ministers said, however, that she presented her resignation "due to the impossibility of reaching consensus for the benefit of the country".\par \par \uc2 The consulting firm \uc2 J.P. Morgan\uc2  said in a statement that Castillo's "lack of skills" to head a government would probably revive the idea that the opposition-dominated Congress would impeach the president again. "We now await the resolution of the political crisis to reassess our forecasts," \uc2 J.P. Morgan\uc2  analysts said in a note.\par \par \uc2 It was unclear whether Economy and Finance Minister Pedro Francke, who has given some calm to investors, would be changed or whether Castillo would ratify him in the post.\par \par \uc2 "If Francke stays and Castillo decides not to opt for more radical left-wing options for his cabinet, the negative market reaction may be short-lived," Citi said in a note on the Peruvian political conjuncture.\par \par \uc2 From the opposition-dominated Congress, mostly right-wing, there were calls to promote a new impeachment process against Castillo, who was spared from an impeachment trial in December that sought to remove him from office.\par \par \uc2 The promoter of the first attempt of "vacancia" of Castillo, legislator Patricia Chirinos of the right-wing Avanza Pa\u237\'00\'EDs party, said that she will present to Congress a new legal initiative to remove the president, who took office in July.\par \par \uc2 The cabinet change will also take place in the midst of a climate of protests against the mining sector and fiscal investigations on alleged corruption in the government's environment.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Benjam\u237\'00\'EDn Mejias and Marco Aquino. Edited by Javier Leira and Daniela Desantis)\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220201ei2100ajq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
