\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Dollar Price LIVE: watch the exchange rate TODAY, Saturday, November 13, 2010\b0\par\par\uc2 554 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 November 2021\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Check the price of the dollar in Peru today, Saturday, November 13, for buying and selling in the parallel market and in the main banks. The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  opened at S/ 4.0208, according to Bloomberg. On Thursday, November 11, the greenback closed at S/4.0190, according to the \uc2 Central Reserve Bank of Peru\uc2  (BCRP).\par \par \uc2 A day earlier, the greenback closed lower at S/$4.0190 on Friday, November 12. The greenback started the day at S/ 4.0214 as reported by the \uc2 Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BCRP), which \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  with the direct sale of US$ 149 million in the whole day. In addition, the closing of Thursday's exchange session represented a significant rise of 0.01% compared to S/ 4.0160 at the close of Wednesday's session, according to BCRP data. Before the end of the day, the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold directly to the market US$ 50 million, at an average value of S/. 4.0180 per dollar. In this way, BCRP accumulates spot purchases for US$ 667 million in November and for US$ 10,689 million this year.\par \par \uc2 In addition, at an economic level, the Executive has on agenda to raise the minimum vital remuneration (RMV) next year, and for this purpose, the trade unions and business associations were summoned to attend this Saturday, at 10:00 a.m. The president has assured that his government will raise the current minimum wage: "As of December, no formal worker will earn less than 1,000 soles a month until the minimum wage is increased," said the head of state.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, the tendency of the dollar to remain stable happens after President Pedro Castillo made his balance for the 100 days of his government in the city of Ayacucho. Among the main issues he dealt with were the second agrarian reform, gas massification and the return to presential classes. In spite of this, according to the president of the Central Reserve Bank (BCRP), Julio Velarde, the Peruvian economy will grow 13.2% this year if the production rhythm observed until August is maintained. During September of this year, the Peruvian economy would also have grown between 8 and 9.5%, said Adri\u225\'00\'E1n Armas, central manager of Economic Studies at the Central Reserve Bank (BCRP).\par \par \uc2 Live: dollar price, exchange rate today, Saturday, November 13 for buying and selling08:1113/11/2021Dollar is at S/ 4.0187, according to BloombergThedollar price today, November 13, is at S/ 4.0187, according to Bloomberg, at 8.00 am. This is lower than the opening price, since Bloomberg put the greenback at S/ 4.0208. It also represents a slight increase from the previous day, when it closed at S/ 4.0180\par \par \uc2 . What is the exchange rate?We use the exchange rate, which is the price of one country's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  (\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) in terms of another, to exchange a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 It isalso known as the exchange rate in other countries.\par \par \uc2 Why is the exchange rate important?Knowing the exchange rate helps us to know how many units of local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  must be paid to obtain a foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . For example, in Peru, to obtain one dollar you must pay approximately three soles and ninety soles.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020211113ehbd00741\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal6