\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Brazilian real, Peru's sol light up gloomy Latam  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 610 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Oktober 2021\par 22:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * Chile's peso slides 1.3%\par     * Peru's sol jumps 1.6%, Brazilian real up 0.4%\par \par  (Updates prices)\par     By Ambar Warrick and Susan Mathew\par     Oct 14 (Reuters) - Brazil's real was supported by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and upbeat economic data on Thursday, while\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Peru\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's sol jumped more than 1% in a winning streak spurred by a\par more moderate shift in left wing President Pedro Castillo's\par government. \par     Most other Latin American \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weakened against the\par dollar after as U.S. economic data fed bets on early tapering by\par the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\par     Chile's peso slumped 1.3%, moving closer towards\par five-month lows hit earlier this week. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reversed\par strong session gains made after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  overnight hiked\par rates by a more-than-expected 125 basis points to 2.75%, amid\par rising inflation.\par     "We stick to our view that (Chile's) policy rate will likely\par peak at 6.00% in 1H22... (but) the evolution of idiosyncratic\par risks will be key to assess how much tightening will be\par necessary," strategists at Citi said. \par     "We think politics will remain the driver for the CLP and\par expect overall weakness into the election."\par     Chile heads to the polls later in November. The opposition\par on Wednesday launched impeachment proceedings against President\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sebastian Pinera\f28 \uc2 \f2  after some details in the Pandora Papers leak.\par \par     Peru's sol hit over 11-week highs, extending gains to\par a sixth straight session - its longest winning streak since\par 2019. It has gained about 5.5% over the six days. \par     The streak started after Mirtha Vasquez was appointed as\par prime minister, replacing far-left \f28 \uc2 \f2 Guido Bellido\f28 \uc2 \f2  whose brash\par style had rattled investors. Some other ministers were also\par replaced with more moderate officials.\par     But the moves did not go down well with his party. The\par ruling Marxist-leaning party Peru Libre on Thursday said it will\par withdraw support for the government in the Congress which is\par dominated by the opposition.\par     The sol is down around 7.6% for year, having slumped since\par the surprise lead and election win for Castillo. It is about 8%\par away from 2021 peaks hit in early April. \par     In Brazil, the real rose 0.4%. After selling $1\par billion worth of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  swaps in a surprise auction on\par Wednesday, the bank said it would hold another sale on Thursday,\par attempting to lift the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from near six-month lows.\par \par     Data on Thursday showed Brazil's services activity grew\par 16.7% in August from last year, indicating some resilience in\par the economy.\par     Latin America's largest economy and most emerging markets\par are under threat from heightened inflation, especially with\par energy prices on the rise.\par      Minutes from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mexican \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's previous meeting\par showed worries about inflation remaining strongly above target,\par while Argentina's inflation rate spiked back up to a\par higher-than-expected 3.5% in September after months of declines.\par \par     Fitch on Thursday affirmed Argentina at 'CCC' in junk grade.\par \par     \par     Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 :\par    Stock indexes           Latest    Daily %\par                                      change\par  MSCI Emerging Markets      1268.28     0.64\par                                      \par  MSCI LatAm                 2244.78     0.73\par                                      \par  Brazil Bovespa           113335.64    -0.11\par                                      \par  Mexico IPC                52168.09     0.69\par                                      \par  Chile IPSA                 3996.48    -0.25\par                                      \par  Argentina MerVal          80066.95     2.09\par                                      \par  Colombia COLCAP            1414.29     1.44\par                                      \par                                             \par       \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2            Latest    Daily %\par                                      change\par  Brazil real                 5.5174     0.36\par                                      \par  Mexico peso                20.5540    -0.03\par                                      \par  Chile peso                     825    -1.14\par                                      \par  Colombia peso               3759.5    -0.58\par                                      \par  Peru sol                     3.918     1.21\par                                      \par  Argentina peso             99.1500    -0.02\par  (interbank)                         \par                                      \par     \par \par  (Reporting by Ambar Warrick; Editing by Giles Elgood and\par Alistair Bell)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2021-10-14T21:09:31.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020211014ehae041wt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\p