ed by the Peruvian Government involving from annual payments for the maintenance and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of the road, which is in charge of the Peruvian Ministry of Transport and Communications (MTC). 99.90% 2032 Financial asset\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Canchaque S.A.C.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 This company operates and periodically maintains a 78 km road which connects the towns of Buenos Aires and Canchaque, in Peru. The road has one toll station. US$31 million Transaction secured by the Peruvian Government regardless the traffic volume. Revenue is secured by an annual minimum amount of US$0.3 million. 99.96% 2025 Financial asset\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Concesionaria. La Chira S.A.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Designing, financing, constructing, operating and maintaining project called 'Planta de Tratamiento de Aguas Residuales y Emisario Submarino La Chira'. The Project will treat approximately 25% of wastewaters in Lima. S/250 million Transaction secured by the Peruvian Government consisting of monthly and quarterly payments settled by Sedapal\u180\'00\'B4s collection trust. 50.00% 2036 Financial asset\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tren Urbano de Lima S.A.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Concession for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Line 1 of Lima Metro, Peru's only urban railway system in Lima city, which includes (i) \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and maintenance of the existing trains (24 initial investment trains and 20 additional trains), (ii) \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and maintenance of the railway system (railway and infrastructure). S/642 million Transaction secured by the Peruvian Government involving a quarterly payment received from MTC based on km travelled per train. 75.00% 2041 Financial asset\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - 57 -\f28 \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1572621/000119312521187240/#toc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Table of Contents}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 Name of\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 concession\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Description\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Estimated\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 investment\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Consideration\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Ordinary\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 shares held Concession\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 termination Accounting\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 model\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Norvial S.A.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Company operates and maintains the highway that connects Lima to the northwest of Peru. This 183 km road known as Red Vial 5 runs from the cities of Ancon to Pativilcaand has three toll stations. US$187\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 million Collected from users (self-financed concession; revenue is derived from collection of tolls). 67.00% 2028 Intangible\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Via Expresa Sur S.A.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Company obtained the concession for designing, financing, building, operating and maintaining the infrastructure associated with the Via Expresa Sur Project. This project involves the second stage expansion of the Via Expresa - Paseo de la Republica,between Av. Republica de Panama and Panamericana highway. US$197\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 million The contract gives the right of collection from users; however the Peruvian Government shall pay the difference when the operating revenue obtained is below US$18 million during the first two years and US$19.7 million from the third year to the fifteenth year of the effective period of the financing, with a ceiling of US$10 million. In June 2017, the contract was suspended temporarily and has been extended until June 2021. To date, the term of the Concession remains suspended by agreement between the parties pending agreement on the terms and conditions to approve the Early Termination of the Concession Contract by Mutual Agreement as provided in Clause 16.3 of the aforementioned Contract. 99.98% 2053 Financial\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ass