uction, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and maintenance of La Chira wastewater treatment plant in the south of Lima. The project is aimed to solve Lima's environmental problems caused by sewage discharged directly into the sea.\par                        \par \par Cumbra Peru S.A.         These joint \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were created exclusively to development of construction contracts.\par                        \par \par UNNA ENERGIA S.A.        Consorcio Terminales and Terminales del Peru provide services for receiving, storing, shipping and transporting liquid hydrocarbons, such as gasoline, jet fuel, diesel fuel and residual among others.\par                        \par \par Concar S.A.C.            Concar's joint \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  provides rehabilitation service, routine and periodic maintenance of the road, and road conservation and preservation services.\par                        \par \par Cumbra Ingenieria S.A.   Engineering consulting services in, study and project execution, project management and Work's supervision.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - 60 -\f28 \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1572621/000119312521187240/#toc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Table of Contents}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 The consolidated financial statements do not include any other type of entities in addition to those mentioned above, such as trust funds or special purpose entities.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 7\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SEGMENT REPORTING\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Operating segments are reported consistently with the internal reports that are reviewed by the Corporation's chief decision-maker; that is, the Executive Committee, which is led by the Corporate General Manager. This Committee acts as the maximum authority in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  decision making and is responsible for allocating resources and evaluating the performance of each operating segment.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Corporation's operating segments are assessed by the activities of the following business units: (i) engineering and construction, (ii) infrastructure, (iii) real estate and (iv) parent company \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As set forth under IFRS 8, reportable segments based on the level of revenue is: 'engineering and construction'. However, the Corporation has voluntarily decided to report in all its operating segments as detailed in this Note.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The revenues derived from foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (Chile, Colombia y Mexico) comprise 24% of the Corporation's total revenue reported in 2020 (19% to 2019).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sales between segments are carried out at arm's length, are not material, and are eliminated on consolidation. The revenue from external parties is measured in a manner consistent with that in the income statement. Sale of goods relate to the real estate segment. Revenue from services relate to all other segments.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Group sales and receivables are not concentrated in a few private customers.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The principal activities of the Corporation in each operating segment are as follows:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 a)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Engineering and construction: This segment includes from traditional engineering services such as structural, civil and design engineering, and architectural planning to advanced specialties including process design, simulation, and environmental services at three divisions; i) civil works, such as the construction of hydroelectric power stations and other large infrastructure facilities; (ii) electro-mechanic construction, such as concentrator plants, oil, and natural gas pipelines, and transmission lines; iii) building construction, such as office buildings, residential buildings, hotels, affordable housing projects, shopping centers, and industrial facilities.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 b)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Infrastructure: The Corporation has long-term concessions or similar contractual arrangements in Peru for three toll roads, the Lima Metro, a wastewater treatment plant in Lima, four producing oil fields, a gas processing plant and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and maintenance services for infrastructure assets.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 c)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Real Estate: The Corporation develops and sells homes targeted to low and middle-income population sectors which are experiencing a significant increase in disposable income, as well as office and commercial space to a lesser extent.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 d)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Parent Company \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : Corresponds to services provided to related entities of the Corporation such as strategic and functional advisory services and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operational\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  leasing of offices.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Executive Committee uses adjusted earnings before interest, tax, depreciation, and amortization (EBITDA) to assess the performance of operating segments. In the years 2019 and 2020, additional provisions have been considered for some of the Corporation\u180\'00\'B4s asses, such as impairment of investments, impairment of account receivables, impairment of goodwill, provision for civil repair and legal claims.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EBITDA is reconciled to operating income (loss) before income taxes as follows (*):\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - 61 -\f28 \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1572621/000119312521187240/#toc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Table of Contents}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2                                                    2019              2020 \par N