ts are December 2021 and October 2023 for Lot I and Lot V, respectively.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 On December 10, 2014, the Peruvian State granted the subsidiary UNNA ENERGIA S.A. the right to exploit for 30 years the oil lots III and IV (owned by the Peruvian State - Perupetro) located in the Talara basin, Piura. The investment committed is estimated at US$400 million and corresponds to the drilling of 230 wells in Lot III and 330 wells in Lot IV. The drilling began in April 2015 in both lots.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As part of the Corporation's obligations under the infrastructure, it is necessary to incur certain costs to prepare the wells located in Lots I, III, IV and V. These costs are capitalized as part of the intangible assets with a value of S/41 million during 2020 (S/108 million in 2019), which includes the capitalization of the provision for dismantling wells and instalations in Lots I, III, IV and V, which during 2020 has not had a significant movement (S/36 million during 2019).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The lots are amortized on the basis of the useful lives of the wells (determined on the remaining terms for lots I and V and units produced for lots III and IV), until the term of contract with Perupetro.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 e)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Amortization of intangible assets\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - 94 -\f28 \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1572621/000119312521187240/#toc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Table of Contents}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 Amortization of intangibles is broken down in the consolidated income statement as follows:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2                                         2019                2020 \par Cost of sales and services (Note 26)              101,810                94,483   \par Administrative expenses (Note 26)                 5,689                  4,138    \par                                                                          \par                                        