8 \par \par \uc2 \f2 With the entry into force of the law 2010 of December 2019 law of economic growth, employment, investment, strengthening of public finances and the progressivity, equity and efficiency of the tax system, the following was stipulated as of January 1, 2020.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The income tax rate applicable to national societies, permanent establishments and foreign legal entities will be 32%, 31% and 30% for the periods 2020,2021 and 2022, respectively.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Payments abroad for interest, commissions, fees, royalties, leases, personal services are subject to withholding tax at the rate of 20%. Payments for consulting, technical services and technical assistance provided by non-residents are subject to the 20% withholding tax rate. Payments for financial returns to non-residents are subject to the 15% withholding tax rate. Payments to the parent company for management fee, are subject to the 33% withholding tax rate.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In case of an increase in taxable income of 30% with respect to the previous year, for fiscal years 2020 and 2021, the statute of limitation of the returns would be six (6) months and in the case of a 20% increase year will be close at month twelve (12).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 c)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The income tax expense shown in the consolidated statement of income comprises (*):\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2                                  2019               2020   \par Current income tax                      114,240              53,134   \par Deferred income tax (Note 24)           189,131              5,310    \par                                                              \par Income tax expense                      303,371              58,444   \par                                                              \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (*) Balances for 2020 were updated as of June 9, 2021\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 d)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Corporation's income tax differs from the th