\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Peru's stock market fails to rebound and drags falabella and Parque Arauco in Chile with new falls\b0\par\par\uc2 366 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Juni 2021\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The Lima Stock Exchange closed its second day yesterday without knowing the name of the new president of Peru.\par \par \uc2 Peru's main stock index, the S&P BVL, struggled to rebound in its first hours of trading, amid statements by presidential candidate Pedro Castillo's top economic adviser, Pedro Francke, seeking to calm the market.\par \par \uc2 However, the index ended up falling 0.55% to 20,385.54 points. Thus, it accumulates a decrease of 8.25% after the elections.\par \par \uc2 central bankMeanwhile, the \uc2 Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the spot dollar market in recent days to mitigate the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rises. Yesterday it went out to sell US$ 81 million at an average exchange rate of 3.982 soles per dollar.\par \par \uc2 "In general, the sun is a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  that has little volatility and Peru is an economy with a lot of predominance of the dollar against the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," explains EuroAmerica investment research analyst Martina Ogaz.\par \par \uc2 "Despite the above, the Peruvian sun has been quite affected by this election, which explains the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he says.\par \par \uc2 Thus, the greenback closed yesterday in the neighboring country with a low of 0.15%, at 3.93 soles.\par \par \uc2 Impact on Chilean actionsOn this side of the border, the Chilean stock market yesterday recovered 0.99% to 4,172.34 points. On Monday it had fallen 2.24%, dragged down by political uncertainty in Peru.\par \par \uc2 Stocks most exposed to that economy again had a session with losses. Falabella was down 0.66%, to $3,030 per paper and Parque Arauco, down 0.32%, to $962 per share.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, \uc2 Enel Americas\uc2  and Entel closed flat.\par \par \uc2 Since the close on Friday before the neighboring country's elections, Parque Arauco's stock has received the greatest impact, with a reduction of 5.03%. It is followed by the declines of 4.93% in Falabella and 3.97% in Entel.\par \par \uc2 In the market they say that the risks in Peru do not necessarily justify reducing positions in these papers, since they would be incorporated into prices.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020210609eh69003fi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
