\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Chile, Peru lead Latam  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  losses; c.bank  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  swap buoys Brazil' real\b0\par\par\uc2 583 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Mai 2021\par 21:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * Potential Chinese price curbs weigh on copper exporters\par     * Brazil c.bank to start $12.2 bln \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  swaps rollover program\par     * Mexico inflation well above \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  target in early\par May\par \par  (Adds comments, bullets; Updates prices throughout)\par     By Susan Mathew and Shreyashi Sanyal\par     May 24 (Reuters) - The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Chile and Peru led\par declines in Latin America on Monday on concerns over curbs on\par industrial metals in top consumer China, while Brazil's real\par recovered from over two-week lows as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \par     Chile's peso fell 1.2%, while \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Peru\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's sol\par dropped 1.5%. A rise in the price of copper was capped after \par China's market regulators warned industrial metal companies to\par maintain "normal market order" during talks on the significant\par gains in metals prices this year.\par     Tensions in Chile regarding the possible overhaul of its\par market-friendly constitution and a likely socialist leadership\par in Peru also have weighed on copper prices. \par     "The (Chilean) government's poor showing in an election to\par decide the relative weight of participation by Chilean political\par parties in a re-write of the country's constitution introduces\par further Chilean asset risk," said Sacha Tihanyi, head of\par emerging markets strategy at \f28 \uc2 \f2 TD Securities\f28 \uc2 \f2 . \par     Brazil's real rose 0.6% after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said\par it will start a program of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  swap auctions on\par Monday that will eventually roll over the $12.2 billion worth of\par traditional swaps contracts due to expire on Aug. 2.\par \par     The political atmosphere in the country grew tenser after\par former leftist and centrist presidents met to try to join forces\par and oppose current far-right leader Jair Bolsonaro in elections\par next year.\par     "With regard to the BRL, it is particularly important to\par watch whether President Bolsonaro flirts with further spending\par packages in an attempt to avoid a drop in his poll prospects,\par and whether fears increase again that the spending cap will be\par undermined," Commerzbank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  analyst Alexandra Bechtel\par said. \par     Data on Monday showed annual headline inflation in Mexico\par stood at 5.80% in the year through the first half of May, well\par above the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's target of 3%, strengthening the case to\par end an easing cycle. The peso rose 0.4%.    \par   \par     In equities, Aeromexico's shares fell 0.2%\par after sources said the \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. government\f28 \uc2 \f2  is preparing to downgrade\par Mexico's aviation safety rating, a move that would bar Mexican\par carriers from adding new U.S. flights and limit airlines'\par ability to carry out marketing agreements.\par \par     Meanwhile on Friday, a closely followed \f28 \uc2 \f2 JPMorgan\f28 \uc2 \f2  survey\par showed investors this month made their biggest cut to "hard\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 " emerging market sovereign bond positions in five\par years.\par  \par     Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 1927 GMT:\par     \par          Stock indexes                 Latest    Daily %\par                                                  change\par  MSCI Emerging Markets                  1327.95    -0.16\par  MSCI LatAm                             2479.07     0.43\par  Brazil Bovespa                       123963.41     1.12\par  Mexico IPC                            49407.19    -0.75\par  Chile IPSA                             4108.24     0.68\par  Argentina MerVal                      56221.87   -1.554\par  Colombia COLCAP                        1226.20    -1.44\par                                                         \par             \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                  Latest    Daily %\par                                                  change\par  Brazil real                             5.3218     0.61\par  Mexico peso                            19.8550     0.39\par  Chile peso                                 730    -1.45\par  Colombia peso                          3732.25     0.33\par  Peru sol                                3.8098    -1.52\par  Argentina peso (interbank)             94.2700    -0.02\par                                                  \par  Argentina peso (parallel)                  150     3.33\par                                                  \par  \par     \par \par  (Reporting by Susan Mathew and Shreyashi Sanyal in Bengaluru;\par Editing by Barbara Lewis and Andrea Ricci)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2021-5-24T20:59:13.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020210524eh5o03b7p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
