\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Former President Jamil Mahuad today presented his book 'So We Dollarize Ecuador'\b0\par\par\uc2 795 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Mai 2021\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Thus we dollarize Ecuador is titled the new book by former President Jamil Mahuad (1997-2000), which was presented on Thursday in a virtual launch by the publisher Ariel of grupo Planeta. The work appears 21 years after the former representative made the economic decision that cost him the office, amid the worst financial crisis in the country's history.\par \par \uc2 "This is the truth written by those who made the decision to dollarize Ecuador, we do not say that it is the only one, but it is the greatest truth and has a virtue: it is the narrative told from within the national government. Over so many years so much has been said about dollarization and they have made a fundamental mistake... they dare to judge how intimate and personal there is, which are people's intentions," Mahuad said at launch.\par \par \uc2 The former president added that he presents the book with pleasure and humility, and that he hopes it could be a contribution to Latin American thinking.\par \par \uc2 Mahuad, currently 71 and based in the USA, participated in the release of his work together with former Presidents Fernando Henrique Cardoso of Brazil and Eduardo Frei of Chile; the president of the Planeta Group, Jos\u233\'00\'E9 Creuheras; and Venezuelan professor and former IDB chief economist Ricardo Haussman. The presentation was by journalist Andrea Bernal.\par \par \uc2 In 1998 and 1999, Ecuador experienced one of the worst economic, social and political crises in the country's history. In this context, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  devaluation and hyperinflation almost lead Ecuador to become a failed state. This was coupled with extreme financial liberalization that led to financial speculation and a subsequent financial institution crisis.\par \par \uc2 The book, in which the former representative sets out what he considers the "memories of a historical success in Latin America", recounts the circumstances that led to one of the most momentous decisions in the country's economic history: dollarization.\par \par \uc2 Henrique Cardoso (1995-2002), recognized the importance of the book and said that he recalled with great satisfaction his \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the process of signing peace between Ecuador and \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 , although he mentioned that it was a complex process and that it took time. On the work in mention, he emphasized that the way it is presented allows for a pleasant reading and that it is accompanied by historical photos that are worth seeing.\par \par \uc2 For his part, former President Frei (1994-2000) emphasized the courage of the former Ecuadorian representative, who he called a great writer, to present this work that is much needed for the political and economic situation at the regional level; He added that, although he is not an economic expert, Ecuador's dollarization was done in a successful way and that is why it has been maintained for more than 20 years.\par \par \uc2 The work has two parts and interactive material through QR codes.\par \par \uc2 The first part of the book is a chronicle, in which Mahuad recounts\u8212\'20\'14 in chronological order, in the first person and with the resources of personal narrative and dialogue\u8212\'20\'14the most significant facts, anecdotes, conversations and reflections of his mandate on the signing of peace with Peru in 1998 (after the 1995 war); and the exchange of the sucre \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the US dollar (the dollarization), in January 2000.\par \par \uc2 The second part is an anthology of texts by members of the government team and consultants of former President Mahuad on various aspects related to the implementation of dollarization in the country. The texts focus on the former (the national and international context, and the reasons that led the Government to study the measure in depth), the during (study of the measure and tensions with the \uc2 IMF\uc2 , the bonistas, Congress and the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Ecuador\uc2 ) and the after (improving revenue, reducing the fiscal deficit and stopping hyperinflation).\par \par \uc2 The back cover of the book includes expert opinions, such as Domingo Cavallo, former minister of Economics, author of the Argentine convertibility plan, who considered that "at the cost of enormous personal sacrifice, Jamil Mahuad provided one of the most lasting solutions to Ecuador's chronic economic instability".\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Haussman recounted that he was able to live closely what Mahuad faced in those years and the effort of resolving tensions on the issue of peace with Peru that was being lived in the country, and then the decision to dollarize the country; he also recalled that Russia's financial collapses at the time and the Asian crisis that caused low oil prices were key to dollarization.\par \par \uc2 "The book leaves the reader a lot of Mahuad lessons. Just to compare, at the same time since Ecuador dollarized, Venezuela has increased twelve zeros to its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , i.e. one million," Haussman said. (I)\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020210513eh5d00a71\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
