\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Dollar in  \highlight22\uc2 Peru \highlight\uc2 : how much would the price have risen without the  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  of the \uc2 BCR\uc2  in the market?\b0\par\par\uc2 453 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 April 2021\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The panorama of uncertainty over the second round starring Pedro Castillo (Peru Libre) and \uc2 Keiko Fujimori\uc2  (People's Force) has had an impact on exchange rate volatility in the last few days, given that for 8 consecutive days the dollar rose to the record level of S/ 3.84 last Monday, April 26.\par \par \uc2 Despite this historic rise, the green banknote could have reached a higher level without careful handling by the Central Reserve Bank (\uc2 BCR\uc2 ), in the opinion of Marco Ortiz, researcher at the Research Center of the University of the Pacific.\par \par \uc2 According to Ortiz, the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  follows a risk management scheme that translates into using exchange rate \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to reduce volatility, so that transient and non-fundamental exchange rate changes do not hit the Peruvian economy too much.\par \par \uc2 It also allows fundamental changes to be reflected in the exchange rate but in an orderly manner, which does not generate too much noise in the markets.\par \par \uc2 The researcher further notes that there are two risks to a small open economy such as Peru's:\par \par \uc2 Exposure to international capital flows and changes in foreign investors' appetite for Peruvian assets, generating volatility in domestic financial marketsThe financial and payment dollarization of Peruvian families, which amplify the impact of exchange change in the economy (balance sheet effects).It should also be noted that the \uc2 BCR\uc2  constantly monitors markets to understand the cause of high volatility. He probably waited for the Fed meeting before deciding to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  more forcefully. With news that U.S. monetary policy would remain expansive, the exchange rate managed to reverse its bullish course and the need for further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was reduced.\par \par \uc2 A simple exercise is to compare \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2  with neighboring countries that are less involved in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets such as Chile and Colombia (although its productive structures have mechanisms that reduce volatility to certain external shocks).\par \par \uc2 The standard deviations from fluctuations in their nominal exchange rates (corrected by trends) have been between 2 and 3 times higher than we experienced in Peru in the last decade.\par \par \uc2 If we simulate a series of the exchange rate for Peru with those values, the exchange rate could have reached levels of S/ 4.70 per dollar instead of the S/ 3.84 recorded. On the other hand, the lowest point of the exchange rate that occurred at the beginning of 2013 of S/ 2.50 per dollar (monthly average), would have been S/ 1.60.\par \par \uc2 Through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, the RB reduces exchange rate volatility by trying to preserve the exchange rate trend in order to avoid the accumulation of external imbalances.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020210430eh4u0073d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
