\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Ecuador bonds rally after surprise election result; c.bank supports Peru's sol\b0\par\par\uc2 616 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 April 2021\par 21:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * Ecuador bonds hit 7-month high \par     * \f28 \uc2 \f2 Guillermo Lasso\f28 \uc2 \f2  wins presidential runoff in Ecuador\par     * Peruvian sol ends flat as cenbank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to stop slide\par     * Far-left Peruvian presidential candidate set to win first\par round\par \par  (Updates prices, adds comment)\par     By Susan Mathew\par     April 12 (Reuters) - Bonds in Ecuador rallied to a seven\par month high on Monday after banker \f28 \uc2 \f2 Guillermo Lasso\f28 \uc2 \f2  pulled off a\par surprise win in Sunday's presidential runoff against socialist\par economist \f28 \uc2 \f2 Andres Arauz\f28 \uc2 \f2 , while \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par cushioned \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Peru\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's sol. \par     The sol and Peruvian stocks had tumbled earlier in the\par session after a far-left candidate, Pedro Castillo, won the\par first round of Peru's presidential election on Sunday.\par     In Ecuador, Lasso took 52% of the vote in a runoff on\par promises to revive the economy, following a campaign that pitted\par his free market economic ideas against the social welfare plans\par of economist Arauz.\par     Ecuador's recently restructured bonds rose sharply, with\par July 2035 paper up 12 cents to 61.6 cents on\par the dollar, a level not seen since September, and the July 2030\par bond up nearly 16 cents to 76 cents on the\par dollar, according to MarketAxess data.\par     "There is little doubt this result reduces short-term\par economic uncertainty," said strategists at Citi Research.\par     However, they added: "Thinking about the medium and long\par terms, our view remains that Ecuador's economic challenges\par (especially on the fiscal front) are very large which, coupled\par with the fact that Lasso did not receive a strong mandate, makes\par us cautious."\par     \par     PERUVIAN JOLT \par     Peru is set for a divisive presidential run-off between its\par ascendant socialists, who have been buoyed by voter discontent\par over the economy and the pandemic, and the conservative heir of\par the powerful but polarizing Fujimori dynasty.  \par     The country's stock index slumped 2% to post its\par worst day in five months, while the sol \par reversed losses to close up 0.11% at 3,617 per dollar after the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to support the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  which fell more\par than 2%.\par     The far-left candidate's success has jolted investors.\par     "Castillo's three pillars are pretty scary. He's talking\par about nationalisation, about the government taking control of\par the economy... it's something that could bring significant\par volatility to the market, just to the bonds overall," said\par Alejandro Arevalo, emerging market debt manager at Jupiter Asset\par Management. \par     Other Latam \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  pared gains and tuned to losses with\par all eyes on U.S. consumer price inflation data, ahead of which\par the dollar traded steady. \par     Brazil's real erased gains to trade almost 1% lower,\par while Mexico's peso traded flat. As oil prices pared some\par gains, crude exporter Colombia's peso extended losses to\par a second day. \par     While most main stock indexes joined a rout in global stocks\par ahead of U.S. inflation data and earnings, Brazil's Bovespa\par index outperformed, up 0.6%, led by financials and\par material stocks. \par     \par     Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 1904 GMT:\par   Stock indexes           Latest   Daily %\par                                    change\par  MSCI Emerging Markets    1320.65    -0.73\par                                    \par  MSCI LatAm               2318.92    -0.77\par                                    \par  Brazil Bovespa         118413.95     0.63\par                                    \par  Mexico IPC              47290.33    -0.71\par                                    \par  Chile IPSA               4944.90    -0.27\par                                    \par  Argentina MerVal        48080.99   -1.566\par                                    \par  Colombia COLCAP          1315.98    -0.46\par                                    \par                                           \par       \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2           Latest   Daily %\par                                    change\par  Brazil real               5.7293    -0.99\par                                    \par  Mexico peso              20.1731    -0.13\par                                    \par  Chile peso                 713.2    -0.22\par                                    \par  Colombia peso            3663.51    -0.15\par                                    \par  Peru sol                  3.6167     0.09\par                                    \par  Argentina peso           92.5700    -0.14\par  (interbank)                       \par                                    \par  \par  (Reporting by Susan Mathew in Bengaluru and Tom Arnold in\par London;\par Editing by Gareth Jones)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2021-4-12T20:24:49.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020210412eh4c03nk5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
