bonds remained close to a maximum of more than a year, causing appetite for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Rising yields and selling bonds globally is seen as a sign of rising inflation. This also stems from investors' fears about the approval of Joe Biden's stimulus plan, with which he will inject money into various sectors of the U.S. economy.\par \par \uc2 In the parallel market or exchange houses of Lima, the exchange rate was quoted at S/ 3,685 the purchase and S/ 3,715 the sale.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020210308eh38007ek\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
