\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Prosecutor's Office  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  as political uncertainty grows in  \highlight22\uc2 Peru \highlight\uc2  and affects the economy\b0\par\par\uc2 696 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 September 2020\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The Peruvian prosecutor's office raided the homes of officials investigated by the contract scandal of a singer this Saturday that caused Congress to approve on Friday to put President \uc2 Mart\u237\'00\'EDn Vizcarra\uc2  on a dismissal trial, a case that already affects an economy in recession by the pandemic.\par \par \uc2 Among the houses registered by prosecutors and police are that of the general secretary of the Peruvian presidency and personal assistant of Vizcarra, Miriam Morales, the civil officer closest to the representative investigated in this case.\par \par \uc2 The homes of presidential office assistant Karem Roca and singer Richard Cisneros, protagonist of this case with rocky dyes, were also raided.\par \par \uc2 Both Morales and Roca are key figures in sneaky-recorded audios in which Vizcarra is heard talking about the scandal and prompting them to lie to the parliamentary committee investigating the case.\par \par \uc2 These audios are the basis of the congressional indictment, which needs 87 votes to dismiss the representative.\par \par \uc2 Against the ropes\par \par \uc2 The representative, who lacks a party and bench, must appear before the plenary on 18 September to offer his discharges, after which the legislators will debate and proceed to vote whether or not to dismiss him.\par \par \uc2 The dissemination of the recordings led six of the nine parties represented in Congress to demand the removal of Biscay, who assumed power in March 2018 following the resignation of \uc2 Pedro Pablo Kuczynski\uc2 , of whom he was vice-president.\par \par \uc2 The decision to bring him to trial was taken on Friday with the vote of 65 lawmakers, 36 against and 24 abstentions, opening a political crisis in a country hard hit by the coronavirus.\par \par \uc2 Economy in distress\par \par \uc2 Political uncertainty has had an effect on the Peruvian economy, which was already facing severe storms over the pandemic.\par \par \uc2 The dollar price closed the last two days rising, accumulating a 7.9% increase in the year due to the pandemic, the recession and now the political crisis.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  closed on Friday at 3,578 suns, a 0.86% rise from the eve, in contrast to 2019, when the exchange rate remained stable throughout the year.\par \par \uc2 To stem the dollar's rise, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  twice on Friday in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has significant macroeconomic strength, a high level of international reserves," said the entity's study manager, Adri\u225\'00\'E1n Armas.\par \par \uc2 "We're going to be prepared to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  and try to just dampen and attenuate any friction or tension that may arise," he added.\par \par \uc2 At the same time, the Lima Stock Exchange closed friday with a fall of 0.42%, while Peru's sovereign bonds fell slightly on the international stock market.\par \par \uc2 Peru's economy is in recession after GDP collapsed 30% in the second quarter, a period that coincided almost entirely with mandatory confinement.\par \par \uc2 In the first quarter it had fallen 3.4% and the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  estimates that this year the contraction will reach 12.5%, the worst figure in three decades.\par \par \uc2 Vizcarra, 57, has had high popularity rates in his two-and-a-half years in power, which was reflected on Friday night in a saucepan in Lima in his support.\par \par \uc2 "I ask Congress to look at the situation cautiously, with responsibility, and make the decision they see fit," Vizcarra said Friday.\par \par \uc2 In supporting the motion before the plenary, opposition lawmaker Jos\u233\'00\'E9 Vega said that these audios "corroborate" the irregularities in the contract to the singer, which Congress has been investigating for months.\par \par \uc2 If dismissed, the head of Congress, Manuel Merino, would rule the remaining 10 months of the current term. Presidential and legislative elections areconvened by April 2021.\par \par \uc2 Prime Minister Walter Martos said Friday that the parliamentary initiative is a "coup d'etating."\par \par \uc2 The crisis erupted when Peru is one of the countries most affected by the pandemic, with more than 716,000 contagions and 30,470 dead.\par \par \uc2 Proportionally to its population, Peru is the most fulsized nation in the world by the coronavirus, with 94.86 death per 100,000 inhabitants, according to the ranking of Johns Hopkins University of the United States.\par \par \uc2 fj/ljc/dga\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020200912eg9c005dz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
