\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 The Peruvian example\b0\par\par\uc2 553 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Februar 2019\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Few countries in the region can exhibit 25 years of continuous growth with monetary stability. After a long history of stagnation, inflation and repeated crises, Peru has succeeded. Their experience should be a lesson for other countries that, like Argentina, can not escape macroeconomic imbalances and a sustained devaluation of their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . A preponderant fraction of our ruling class and citizens disapprove of the successful policies of other countries. On the contrary, it supports populist approaches and heterodox programs that guarantee failure. An ideological enclosure prevents objectivity in the evaluation and analysis of concrete experiences. Close cases like those of Chile and \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2  are voluntarily ignored. Peruvian governments developed populist, \b \highlight22\uc2 interventionist\b0 \highlight\uc2  and statist policies during the 1960s, 1970s and 1980s. They were the ones demanded by the bulk of the leadership and the intelligentsia and that were accepted by the military and civilian governments.\par \par \uc2  As it could not happen otherwise, the fiscal deficit exceeded the possibilities of financing itself with debt and the issuance of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Central Reserve Bank (BCRP) had to be resorted to. But it was not just the only source of money creation. The BCRP acted as a development bank, granting loans to other state banks, which in turn lent to state and private companies on advantageous terms, with weak guarantees and weak possibilities to deal with financial services. Since the mid-1970s, inflation accelerated and during the presidency of Alan Garc\u237\'00\'EDa hyperinflation was reached. Between 1985 and 1990, prices accumulated an increase of 6,921,502%. Between 1987 and 1990 the fiscal deficit averaged 10.5% of GDP, and the economy was reduced by 25%. However, in Buenos Aires the street propaganda of the workers' union in the Christmas week asked Santa Claus "a president like Alan Garc\u237\'00\'EDa". The hyperinflationary trauma and the proven uselessness of the control of prices and changes led to a modification of the prevailing opinions. President \uc2 Alberto Fujimori\uc2 , elected in 1990, thus had the necessary support to reorient economic policy and regularize the financial situation with multilateral organizations and private creditors. A new Constitution was approved by referendum in 1993, as well as the modification of the BCRP charter. The \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  set its exclusive objective to preserve the value of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by defeating inflation. The effects of the change have been remarkable. The fiscal deficit was reduced and controlled. Between 1993 and 2018, annual inflation averaged 4.2% and annual GDP growth averaged 5%. The BCRP works with the inflation targeting system and does it successfully and profitably. This is possible within the framework of a controlled fiscal situation, which did not happen in Argentina and determined its failure. Alan Garc\u237\'00\'EDa was elected again in 2001 and proved to have learned the lesson. In his second government he executed a pro-market policy and fiscal and monetary discipline. Learning from one's mistakes is a quality that has not yet reached a large part of our politicians. Nor do they seem to have learned from the experiences, mistakes and successes of other countries and governments. The prolonged Peruvian success, based on the total independence of its \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the stability of its authorities, should be a case of study and more than recommended.\par \par \uc2 Copyright Grupo de Diarios Am\u233\'00\'E9rica - GDA / La Naci\u243\'00\'F3n / Argentina\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020190215ef2f003bh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
