\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Peru \highlight\uc2 's Sol to Remain Steady on  \highlight22\uc2 Interventions \highlight\uc2  -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 943 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Februar 2018\par 13:43\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2018, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 1143 GMT - \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 's sol \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  probably won't see big swings in its exchange rate against the dollar in 1H18 as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will likely continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to prevent appreciation from stronger copper prices, says BMI Research. In the short term, the sol will likely stay around 3.24 per greenback, firm says. Longer term, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should ease its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , allowing the sol to strengthen slightly to 3.2 by year-end thanks to stronger copper prices, BMI says. Copper is Peru's top export earner. The sol closed last week at 3.252 per dollar, according to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . (ryan.dube@wsj.com; @duberyan)\par \par \uc2 1140 GMT - \uc2 Warren Buffett\uc2  is outspoken on politics, but he doesn't want to impose his political views on Berkshire's investment decisions or business \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he says on CNBC. Berkshire doesn't own any gun manufacturers, he says, but there is no rule that they wouldn't. And he points out that though he doesn't think cigarettes are good, Berkshire's subsidiary McLane distributes cigarettes to retailers like \uc2 Walmart\uc2  . Some companies have cut ties to the \uc2 National Rifle Association\uc2  in response to pressure from students following a Florida high-school shooting. "I think what the kids are doing is very admirable, but I don't think Berkshire should say we're not going to do business with people who own guns. I think that would be ridiculous," Buffett says. (nicole.friedman@wsj.com; @NicoleFriedman)\par \par \uc2 1126 GMT - When asked on CNBC about continuing issues at \uc2 Wells Fargo\uc2  , Warren Buffett repeats lines he has used before. He says that Wells had bad incentives in place and that the company's management erred by not responding quickly enough when alerted to problems. He also compared the issue to the issues at Salomon in the early 1990s, when Buffett took over the troubled company as interim chairman. He does say that he thinks Wells's problems are in the past: "What my guess is, is that they have scrubbed and scrubbed and they have found out the things that they have done wrong. And the Fed and any other supervisor is going to make them pay, which they have." (nicole.friedman@wsj.com; @NicoleFriedman)\par \par \uc2 1122 GMT - \uc2 Warren Buffett\uc2  demurs somewhat on commenting on \uc2 General Electric\uc2  's recent issues on CNBC, but he does say: "There were mistakes made....The accounting at GE has not been a model at all in recent years." Long-term care insurance has been a problem for many insurance companies, including his own \uc2 Berkshire Hathaway\uc2  , Buffett says, but he was "staggered" by the extent of the long-term care insurance problems at GE, he says. Berkshire sold its GE stock at $29, he says. The stock is currently trading at $14.53. (nicole.friedman@wsj.com; @NicoleFriedman)\par \par \uc2 1116 GMT - Net sales were down in all geographic segments in \uc2 Welbilt\uc2 's latest quarter. Total net sales fall 3.4% to $365.9M. While the company does the most in sales in North America, sales in the Asia-Pacific region declined the fastest, dropping 8.2% to $51.8M. Analysts polled by \uc2 Thomson Reuters\uc2  were expecting revenue of $383.6M. \uc2 Welbilt\uc2  also announced plans Monday morning to buy coffee-maker company Crem International, a deal \uc2 Welbilt\uc2  CEO \uc2 Hubertus Muehlhaeuser\uc2  says supports \uc2 Welbilt\uc2 's plans to grow in Europe and Asia, where "Crem is very strong." (allison.prang@wsj.com; @AllisonPrang)\par \par \uc2 1110 GMT - With Berkshire's cash pile growing to $116B at the end of 2017, pressure is mounting on chairman \uc2 Warren Buffett\uc2  to return capital to shareholders. Buffett says on CNBC that he thinks Berkshire will find better uses for the money, but if it does give money back to shareholders, it will likely to do via buybacks, not dividends. "The inclination might be more toward repurchase than dividends, because dividends have the implied promise that you keep paying them forever," he says. Berkshire already has said it would repurchase shares if prices fall to 120% of book value or below, and Buffett says that threshold could rise in the future. "We would do what made the most sense for shareholders." ( nicole.friedman@wsj.com, @NicoleFriedman)\par \par \uc2 1108 GMT - \uc2 Warren Buffett\uc2  says on CNBC that in this year's March Madness bracket tournament for \uc2 Berkshire Hathaway\uc2  employees, the prize will be doubled if Creighton or Nebraska wins the tournament. The company offers a $100,000 prize for the employee whose bracket lasts the longest. And if any employee gets the entire Sweet 16 correctly, they win $1M a year for life -- or if \uc2 Creighton\uc2  or Nebraska wins, now it would be $2M a year for life, says Buffett, a Nebraska native. Last year a West Virginia employee of Berkshire subsidiary \uc2 Precision Castparts\uc2  won the contest. (nicole.friedman@wsj.com; @NicoleFriedman)\par \par \uc2 1050 GMT - \uc2 Dechra Pharmaceuticals\uc2  posted strong first-half FY 2018 results, growing sales and expanding margins, says \uc2 Numis\uc2 , lifting its forecasts for the animal medicine company. \uc2 Dechra\uc2  says its strong performance in North America, where sales were up 18%, helped boost its revenue 13%, and \uc2 Numis\uc2  says the company saw gross margins improve to 55.9% from 53.4%, in line with expectations. Meanwhile, \uc2 Numis\uc2  also says the company's selling, general and administrative expenses were better than expected. The broker lifts its EPS forecasts by 4% to 5% for FY 2018 and FY 2019, respectively. (carlo.martuscelli@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 February 26, 2018 07:43 ET (12:43 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020180226ee2q001k8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
