\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-\uc2 Peru  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  leaves key rate unchanged as inflation eases\b0\par\par\uc2 332 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juli 2016\par 01:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's comments, details throughout)\par \par \uc2 LIMA, July 14 (Reuters) - \uc2 Peru's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  held the benchmark interest rate steady at 4.25 percent for the fifth straight month as expected on Thursday after inflation continued to cool toward its target ceiling.\par \par \uc2 All 13 economists polled by Reuters had forecast the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would keep the key rate unchanged.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said that in making its decision it took into consideration that inflation expectations continue to gradually ease, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and food product and public service price increases has been reversing, and domestic economic activity is growing at close to its potential.\par \par \uc2 Earlier on Thursday the head of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  described current monetary policy as "nearly neutral, slightly expansive."\par \par \uc2 The annual inflation rate dropped to 3.34 percent in June from 3.54 percent in May, closer to the upper limit of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's target range of 1 to 3 percent.\par \par \uc2 In its post-meeting statement, the bank said it is vigilant of inflation expectations in considering possible future adjustments to the monetary policy rate. "Inflation is expected to be within the target range before year end," said the bank.\par \par \uc2 The sol's 14.6 percent depreciation last year helped push inflation to a four-year high of 4.4 percent in January. But the sol has gained nearly 4 percent against the dollar so far in 2016, even as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has stepped up its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local spot market.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 's mining-dependent economy has been recovering since late last year on the back of surging copper output from new mines, but domestic demand has remained relatively weak.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has forecast an uptick in growth in May and June and expects a 4 percent economic expansion this year. (Reporting by Teresa Cespedes; Writing by Mitra Taj & Anthony Esposito; Editing by Peter Cooney and Diane Craft) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-7-15T00:36:56.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020160714ec7e017od\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
