\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Peru central bank \highlight\uc2  wary of U.S. rate hike, defends  \highlight22\uc2 interventions \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 477 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 August 2015\par 23:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  says has plenty of reserves to soften sol's slide               \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  aim to tame inflation and protect recovery               \par \par \uc2 * Velarde says \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  depreciation should ease after Fed hike   (Recasts to focus on Velarde's defense of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , adds comments on inflation, economic recovery)               \par \par \uc2 By Teresa Cespedes               \par \par \uc2 LIMA, Aug 19 (Reuters) - The chief of \uc2 Peru's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday defended the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 's nearly daily \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, citing its increasing uneasiness over an expected interest rate hike in the United States.               \par \par \uc2 "We really have growing fears with respect to the impact on the withdrawal of monetary stimulus in the U.S.," Julio Velarde told reporters on the sidelines of an event.               \par \par \uc2 Velarde said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  still has plenty of dollar reserves it can sell in the spot market to soften the sol's   losses against the dollar.               \par \par \uc2 The bank bought some $13 billion in 2012 when the sol was appreciating. Since then, it has sold less than $10 billion, he said.               \par \par \uc2 "We still haven't used what we bought during the last year the sol was strengthening," Velarde said.               \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has ramped up its dollar sales in recent weeks. It sold more than half a billion in the past week as the sol has set a new six-year low daily.               \par \par \uc2 Velarde said the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  were needed to tame inflation that is sensitive to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swings in \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 .               \par \par \uc2 "The reason we \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  is because credits ... and prices ... are still highly dollarized," Velarde said.               \par \par \uc2 He said abrupt \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  changes also threaten the economic recovery.               \par \par \uc2 Peru's economy, which is fueled by mining, expanded by 3 percent in the second quarter on the year, the best pace in more than a year. But annual growth of 1.92 percent in June was well below the potential rate the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  put at 5 percent in February.               \par \par \uc2 "We're seeing that the potential growth rate is falling," Velarde said. "At times when the economy is weak, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  changes shouldn't be so brusque."               \par \par \uc2 Velarde said the sol's recent losses were due to rampant speculation that would likely continue until the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  raises interest rates. Afterward, "there should be no reason for the exchange rate to rise further," he said.               \par \par \uc2 "We think the market has gotten ahead of itself. I personally think it is very ahead of itself," Velarde added.                              \par \par \uc2 Velarde's comments follow the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's announcement last week that it was considering raising the interest rate next month to counter \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -driven inflationary pressures.               \par \par \uc2 Velarde said a rate hike in Peru was far from guaranteed.               \par \par \uc2 "It's going to depend on the data we see - August inflation, the pace of economic activity, impacts on inflation expectations," he said.               \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-8-19T22:54:19.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150819eb8j00sxx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
