\par\par \b \uc2 Peru  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Sells More Dollars to Support Sol -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,323 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Juni 2015\par 21:36\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 15:36 EDT - The \uc2 Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market today, selling $83M in US dollars, once again aiming to ease depreciation pressures on the sol. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has sold $309M in the last three trading sessions as the Peruvian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  falls out of favor. The sol has weakened 6.44% against the US dollar so far this year. USD/PEN last at 3.172. (robert.kozak@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 15:16 EDT - \uc2 Ikea\uc2 's US workforce is getting its second significant wage hike in as many years, a move that comes after retailers like \uc2 McDonald's\uc2  (MCD), Target (TGT) and \uc2 Wal-Mart\uc2  (WMT) all have bumped up hourly wages for store-level workers in recent month. While \uc2 Ikea\uc2  does look at the local competition for workers, the latest 10% hike isn't driven by that. The furniture retailer uses a living wage calculator to determine wages, and as that has gone up this past year, so are wages. "We're not naive to not look at competition but that's not the impetus to the overall change," says Rob Olson, CFO of Ikea's US division. (paul.ziobro@wsj.com; @pziobro)\par \par \uc2 15:07 EDT - Congress is moving to close a loophole that has helped for-profit colleges grab an even larger chunk of taxpayer dollars than they otherwise might have. Three Democratic Senators today announced new legislation that would mean federal education benefits for military personnel would count against a rule that limits for-profit colleges from generating more than 90% of their tuition dollars from federal loans. That loophole had encouraged marketing campaigns targeting veterans. One company that enrolls a large number of them is American Public Education (APEI), which warns in \uc2 SEC\uc2  filings that such legislation could harm its business. The industry has already been hammered as regulators have discovered a litany of abuses, including low graduation rates and high loan default rates. (rolfe.winkler@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 15:06 EDT - \uc2 Unilever\uc2 's deal to buy skin care company Dermalogica is another step in the consumer giant's journey to skew its brand portfolio towards the more high-margin business of personal care. The deal follows \uc2 Unilever\uc2 's recent acquisitions of REN and Kate Somerville. Dermalogica is sold in more than 80 countries worldwide with the US, UK, Australia, Canada and Germany being its major markets. No doubt more "bolt on" style acquisitions to come from \uc2 Unilever\uc2  in skin and haircare. Terms of the deal weren't disclosed. (saabira.chaudhuri@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 14:59 EDT - Recent declines in the US unemployment rate have been driven more by job creation than discouraged workers giving up the search, \uc2 Deutsche Bank\uc2  says. That's why as improving conditions lure job-seekers back into the labor market, the firm sees that having limited impact in pushing up the jobless rate. Using figures from the May jobs report, DB says if all Americans labeled non-participants who would take a job now were marked instead as unemployed but actively seeking jobs, the labor force would have had an additional 717k unemployed workers. That would have added just 0.4 point to the reported 5.5% unemployment rate. (cynthia.lin@wsj.com; @cynthialin_dj)\par \par \uc2 14:56 EDT - \uc2 Steven Nell\uc2 , CFO of BOK Financial (BOKF) for the past 14 years, shot to No. 3 on the list of the most highly paid bank and thrift CFOs last year, according to a study from \uc2 SNL Financial\uc2 . Nell received total 2014 compensation valued at $8.2M. That put him behind only \uc2 Bank of America\uc2 's (BAC) \uc2 Bruce Thompson\uc2  with $11.6M, and \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2 's (\uc2 JPM\uc2 ) \uc2 Marianne Lake\uc2  with $9.1M. Nell's $4.5M bonus and $490,700 salary gave him the highest cash takeaway in the top 10. His total compensation was valued at more than six-and-a-half times what he received a year earlier. (maxwell.murphy@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 14:50 EDT - As promised as part of the deal that saved more than 1,700 stores from bankruptcy liquidation, the defunct retailer long known as \uc2 RadioShack\uc2  has officially changed its name. It's now calling itself RS Legacy Corp. An affiliate of lender Standard General bought the core of the business in chapter 11, including the name, leaving cash and battling creditors behind in bankruptcy court. The revived store chain goes by the name of \uc2 RadioShack\uc2 , while RS Legacy Corp., the shell left behind in bankruptcy, sorts through cash and unpaid bills in an effort to wrap up the old company's affairs. (peg.brickley@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 14:34 EDT - The \uc2 International Finance Corp\uc2 . is teaming up with coffee trader Ecom, \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  (SBUX) and the \uc2 Inter-American Development Bank\uc2  to provide long-term loans to Nicaraguan coffee growers hit by the rust fungus "roya" that has hurt production across Central America. IFC, part of the \uc2 World Bank\uc2 , will put up $12M of the $30M loan program, as will the IDB. \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  and Ecom will each provide $3M. "Income losses for farmers in Central America have been compounded by lower global coffee prices due to bumper crops in other regions, and the chronic lack of long-term financing is a constraint," says IFC, which then intends to extend the program to other countries. Roya has affected up to 70% of plantations in some countries, IFC says. (anthony.harrup@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 14:30 EDT - Ahold Chief Executive Dick Boeras said in an interview that the U.S., its largest market, is increasingly competitive, putting pressure on grocery stores to cut costs and use the savings to differentiate themselves. Ahold's plan to merge with Delhaize, he says, adds scale, which allows them to invest more in innovation. Both companies have worked on adjusting their prices and adding more store brands and fresh produce in recent years. "In the U.S., we can accelerate that improvement level to make it a better shopping experience for customers," added Delhaize Chief Executive \uc2 Frans Muller\uc2 . "There are plenty of things to do in this fast-changing landscape." (annie.gasparro@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 14:26 EDT - Nearly a year into its second bankruptcy case, \uc2 Revel AC\uc2 , the former owner of the Revel Casino Hotel in Atlantic City, NJ, has spent $15.8M on fees and expenses for attorneys and other professionals, according to court papers filed Tuesday. The majority of that went to pay \uc2 White & Case\uc2 , Revel's primary bankruptcy counsel. Revel, a gleaming, 47-story boardwalk tower, filed its second chapter 11 case in June 2014. The resort, which cost $2.4B to build, has since been sold to Florida-based developer \uc2 Glenn Straub\uc2  for $82M. (tom.corrigan@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 14:13 EDT - Research cited by a \uc2 New York Fed\uc2  official today shows that emerging-market capital flows are disproportionately hit when market participants are surprised by policy moves. Unanticipated Fed tightening moves have resulted in private capital providers pulling back from emerging markets to four times the extent they would in a normal tightening cycle, the official says. "This highlights the importance of transparency and clear messaging by the Fed about how it is evaluating the economic landscape, to reduce the risk that policy adjustments might be associated with undue market volatility," says \uc2 Alberto Musalem\uc2 , executive vice president at the \uc2 New York Fed\uc2  at a banking industry conference. (katy.burne@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 14:03 EDT - \uc2 Fiat\uc2  Chrysler (FCAU) CEO \uc2 Sergio Marchionne\uc2  says the Italian-American car maker will file documents for Ferrari's IPO in a few weeks. Marchionne, speaking at the presentation of a new Alfa Romeo sedan, has said the sale of a 10% stake will take place in 4Q. He hasn't indicated which investment banks will lead the offering. (eric.sylvers@wsj.com; @EricSylvers)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 June 24, 2015 15:36 ET (19:36 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020150624eb6o002vo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
