\par\par \b \uc2 Peru  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Steps in to Support Sol -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,386 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Mai 2015\par 22:51\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 16:51 EDT - \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continues to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to support the sol, which has depreciated 12.5% over the last year against the US dollar. The central reserve bank today sells $25M at an average of PEN3.151 per dollar. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  says it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth out volatility in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. USD/PEN at 3.149 from 2.984 at the start of the year. (robert.kozak@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 2049 GMT - The upcoming April Australia labor-market report is a major focus for NZD investors, with about 4k in employment gains expected and the unemployment rate seen rising from 6.1% to 6.2%. While Wednesday's New Zealand jobs data undermined NZD "offshore markets are still dominant with a weak US \uc2 ADP\uc2  employment and a continued sell-off in global long-end yields keeping NZD/USD relatively stable around 0.75," says \uc2 ANZ Bank\uc2 . The pair is at 0.7503 and it tips a range of 0.7460-0.7580. (rebecca.howard@wsj.com; @FarroHoward)\par \par \uc2 16:48 EDT - \uc2 Whole Foods (WFM) \uc2 reported earnings that beat expectations, but its gross margin continue to struggle and same-store sales growth for the past five weeks was just 2.8%, down from historic averages of 7%-8%. The specialty chain has struggled for several quarters but said in February its efforts to improve value were paying off and sales trends were improving. The latest quarter, and today's announcement that \uc2 Whole Foods\uc2  will launch a new store concept based on offering better value, signals that its business model could be faltering. Shares sink 11% after hours to $42.40. (annie.gasparro@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 16:39 EDT - Brazil's economic activity is running much worse than anybody has anticipated, and even the \uc2 Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will likely soon be forced to revise lower its forecast for GDP growth in 2015, \uc2 Espirito Santo Investment Bank\uc2  says. Industrial production declined 0.8% in March, more than economists had expected. The gauge has been on a decline since mid-2013. The bank believes the weak backdrop for economic growth will limit the degree of monetary tightening. Last week, \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised its benchmark interest rate to 13.25% from 12.75%. (luciana.magalhaes@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 16:28 EDT - With 1Q results a hair below Wall Street targets, TripAdvisor's (TRIP) most interesting story lies in its non-core businesses. Revenue from subscriptions, transactions and other sources jumped 88% to $79M, showing its pays to stray outside the online travel company's comfort zone. TRIP has bought a string of dining, tourism and vacation sites to broaden its base beyond ads that lead to hotel bookings, its bread and butter. Alternative revenue now makes up roughly 1/5 of its top line. TRIP climbs 3.5% to $79.50 after hours. (andrew.fitzgerald@wsj.com; @drewfitzgerald)\par \par \uc2 2028 GMT - The New Zealand dollar "holds the dubious honor of being the only G10 \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken against the USD over the (overnight) session, thanks to [Wednesday's] employment report," says BNZ \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Raiko Shareef. He notes while the RBNZ signalled it wants to see prices and wages settle at lower levels "investors are not waiting around to find out, and quite appropriately moved to price in a greater chance of rate cuts in 2015." The kiwi is "significantly weaker" against rivals, with the decline against EUR particularly big, he says. NZD/AUD extends lower, with key support at the 200-day moving average (0.9340) within striking distance. "Momentum suggests some further downward movement, but we maintain that a broad 0.92-0.98 range will prevail through year-end." NZD/AUD at 0.9426. NZD/EUR is at 0.6618. (rebecca.howard@wsj.com; @FarroHoward)\par \par \uc2 16:23 EDT - As retailers get set to report earnings over the next few weeks, Janney worries that consumer stocks might have gotten a little ahead of themselves. "We will be watching for clues...the cycle is getting into the late innings," the firm writes. Janney below the Street on several large retailers, including \uc2 Wal-Mart\uc2  (WMT), arguing that investments in labor, pricing and IT will cut into earnings, and Target (TGT), where expectations have risen quickly and also their need to cut prices more. \uc2 Home Depot\uc2  (HD) and Lowes (LOW) both will like do well, but Janney wonders whether their high valuations can go any higher. (paul.ziobro@wsj.com; @pziobro)\par \par \uc2 16:18 EDT - Increased attention from regulators is changing the cyberinsurance market for insurers and their customers, said Lynda Bennett, chair of the insurance coverage practice at law firm \uc2 Lowenstein Sandler\uc2 . Until recently insurers grappled with how to underwrite, how to ask the right questions before issuing insurance policies, she said. But new requirements coming from the \uc2 Financial Industry Regulatory Authority\uc2  and the SEC that broker-dealers and eventually public companies make disclosures of what they are doing to be prepared for cyberattacks "will show insurers these companies are better risks to take on than companies not subject to the same level of regulation," said Ms. Bennett. (ben.dipietro@wsj.com; @bendipietro1)\par \par \uc2 16:07 EDT - US stocks fall for a second straight session as Fed Chairwoman \uc2 Janet Yellen\uc2  says stock market valuations appear somewhat elevated and some bond and loan markets suggest investors may be taking excess risks. Comments added to jitters following a weak reading from the \uc2 ADP\uc2  private payrolls ahead of Friday's jobs report for April, which could help sway the timing of the Fed's rate hike plans. DJIA slips 86 points to 17841, after briefly trading into negative territory for the year. \uc2 S&P 500\uc2  loses 9 to 2080 and the \uc2 Nasdaq\uc2  drops 19 to 4919. Treasurys extend recent weakness, with the 10-year yield near its highest level of the year. (patrick.sullivan@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 16:06 EDT - Minutes from Brazil's last monetary policy meeting, scheduled for release Thursday, will likely show the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continuing to project above-target inflation this year and next despite weaker economic growth, \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2  says. Last week, \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised its benchmark interest rate to 13.25% from 12.75%. In the 12 months through mid-April, consumer prices in Brazil rose 8.22%, above the ceiling of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's target range of 2.5% to 6.5%. \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will likely reiterate that progress in fighting inflation has been insufficient and likely indicate that's not done tightening, BNP says. Firm sees rates peaking at 14% in July and staying there until the end of the year. (luciana.magalhaes@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 15:59 EDT - Just as the rail industry poises itself to challenge a new DOT rule mandating expensive oil train upgrades, including a new braking system for longer trains, a BNSF train carrying crude derails. The North Dakota incident brings the total to at least nine fiery oil train derailments since 2013. "Today's incident is yet another reminder of why we issued a significant, comprehensive rule aimed at improving the safe transport of high hazard flammable liquids," Acting Federal Railroad Administrator Sarah Feinberg says. It's unclear what caused today's incident or whether it could have been prevented by the new brakes. Still, the rail industry has contended that the new braking system won't prevent derailments and a loophole could dramatically reduce network capacity. (laura.stevens@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 15:59 EDT - U.S. beer business started the year slowly, but warmer weather in March helped boost volume. Tax paid shipments increased 2% in March to 15 million barrels, a 300,000 barrel increase from March 2014, according to the \uc2 Beer Institute\uc2 . That represented a major improvement from January and February when shipments were down 6.4% and 7.1% respectively. Beer Marketer's Insights, which tracks the industry, said that the slow start was "far from insurmountable." \uc2 AB InBev\uc2  (BUD) on Wednesday reported shipments-to-retailers decreased just 0.5% in the first quarter. \uc2 MillerCoors\uc2  co-owner Molson Coors (TAP) reports earnings May 7. (tripp.mickle@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 May 06, 2015 16:51 ET (20:51 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020150506eb560049m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
