\par\par \b \uc2 UBS\uc2  Stays Bullish on Oilfield Majors -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,308 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2015\par 14:31\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 8:31 EST - \uc2 UBS\uc2  says oil prices should slowly move higher into 2016-7, to $65-70/barrel, as it defends its buy ratings on the world's four largest oilfield-services companies--\uc2 Schlumberger\uc2  (SLB), \uc2 Halliburton\uc2  (HAL), \uc2 Baker Hughes (BHI) \uc2 and Weatherford (WFT). It acknowledges pricing and oversupply will challenge the quartet and that oil prices are key. "As in every downcycle/recovery, EPS, rig count and multiples become less important as oil prices dictate the industry outlook and stock performance." Their stocks have fallen to varying degrees the past 6 months, with BHI off just 8% amid its pending purchase by HAL, which is down 35%. SLB has fallen 20% and WFT has slumped 48%. (dan.molinski@wsj.com; @dmwsj)\par \par \uc2 8:27 EST - Private payrolls added 212,000 in February, says \uc2 ADP\uc2  today, close to the 215,000 gain expected by economists. That suggests few or no forecasters will change their number for Friday's payrolls report. The consensus calls for the Labor Department to report a solid gain of 240,000 nonfarm jobs (which include government slots) and the February unemployment rate to fall to 5.6% from 5.7% in January. (kathleen.madigan@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 8:27 EST - February may have proved to have been a yin-yang month for \uc2 McDonald's\uc2  (MCD) US sales, says Janney as it goes from 1% same-store-sales growth to a 1% decline ahead of Monday's report. "Clearly, part of the very-positive first half of February reflects favorable year-over-year weather. And just as clearly, part of the much-more-challenging second half of February reflects unfavorable year-over-year weather." (kevin.kingsbury@wsj.com; @kevinkingsbury)\par \par \uc2 8:24 EST - Treasury prices perk up after the in-line \uc2 ADP\uc2  employment report, which admittedly hasn't been a stable predictor of the government's data. That print Friday will be the key release ahead of the FOMC meeting on March 17-8, the focus of which being whether patience is removed. The yield on the 10-year Treasury is 2.108%, versus 2.122% Tuesday. (min.zeng@wsj.com; @minzengwsj)\par \par \uc2 8:07 EST - As Abercrombie (ANF) continues to struggle, fellow teen-apparel retailer American Eagle (AEO) says F4Q EPS rose even more than anticipated as it gives an above-consensus 1Q forecast despite anticipated West Coast port impacts to the bottom line. Helping year-end results were "improved merchandise" and fewer promotions, says CEO \uc2 Jay Schottenstein\uc2 . AEO's same-store sales were flat in 4Q, which is actually decent considering how things have been in the space, and gross margin surged 3.2 percentage points to 35.1%. Inventory is also in check, down 5% from a year earlier on a cost/foot basis. AEO jumps 6.3% premarket to $15.75, which would be a 15-month high. ANF is now down 6.6% to what would be a fresh 6-year low. (kevin.kingsbury@wsj.com; @kevinkingsbury)\par \par \uc2 7:54 EST - Banco de Credito sees more volatility ahead for the Peruvian sol, saying it could take place in the gap between \uc2 Peru's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meeting on March 12 and the following week's FOMC gathering. \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been actively \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market by selling dollars (including $303M Monday) to ease volatility. Banco de Credito says the activity and an improved price for copper have eased depreciation pressures on the sol. (robert.kozak@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 7:53 EST - Share buybacks have been a key source of stock gains and earning growth, and they look set to continue, analyst Ed Yardeni says, for the simple reason that it makes economic sense. Corporate bond yields have been and remain below the forward earnings yield for the \uc2 S&P 500\uc2 , he says, a phenomenon that has driven $2.1 trillion in buybacks from 2009 through 3Q 2014. Buybacks could mean 1H earnings growth for the index, now expected to be negative, could in fact turn in a positive reading. (andrew.dowell@dowjones.com; @drewdowell)\par \par \uc2 7:51 EST - Treasury prices are little changed after two days of selling as today's US data loom, starting in minutes with \uc2 ADP\uc2 's employment report. Still, the key one is Friday's nonfarm-jobs print, which should further shape expectations on the Fed's rate outlook. This week, Treasurys have been hit by a flurry of new corporate-bond sales. More are scheduled by week's end. The yield on the 10-year Treasury is at 2.12%, versus 2.122% Tuesday. (min.zeng@wsj.com; @minzengwsj)\par \par \uc2 7:45 EST - Weather hit the auto industry in February, but \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2 's \uc2 Adam Jonas\uc2  reflected other analysts in calling the softness a "minor hiccup." Volumes should come roaring back in March, as buyers come out of hibernation. The trend to watch? Transaction prices, which have increased eight straight months. Sales, Jonas says, "continue to punch above their weight on the value side. Disciplined use of incentives and demand for trucks and luxury are fueling this trend. But will it last? Don't be so sure. "Jumping forward to spring, we expect to see more accommodative/competitive financing. This will push volumes to 17M, but eventually there will be a "tab to pay when the string runs out." (john.stoll@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 7:45 EST - \uc2 Google\uc2  (GOOGL) is losing its lock on location services. Uber's acquisition of \uc2 deCarta\uc2 , a mapping company, allows it to potentially distance itself from GOOGL. The two companies are on the one hand tied together--\uc2 Google Ventures\uc2  invests in Uber and a GOOGL executive sits on Uber's board. But on the other hand, GOOGL could become a competitor with self-driving cars. At the same time, \uc2 Samsung\uc2  (005930.SE) seems to be heavily promoting its own location services, says IHS Technology's Gerrit Schneemann. He notes the South Korean firm has prominently showed off its MirrorLink auto services and unveiled technology which would let a \uc2 Samsung\uc2  user tie together a phone, wearable device and car. (lisa.fleisher@wsj.com; @lisafleisher)\par \par \uc2 7:41 EST - Wondering how Tesla (TSLA) is doing this quarter? Finding a reliable answer will be tough. The company doesn't break out monthly volumes, but the situation is closely watched after TSLA reported disappointing 4Q volumes and said this quarter would benefit. Two firms which estimate the auto maker's sales have wildly different views. Autodata says TSLA's US sales were 1,200 last month, down 25%, with the estimated 2-month figure down 29% at 2,200. But while WardsAuto.com puts sales below Autodata, it says they've grown from year-earlier levels. WardsAuto estimates TSLA's February sales jumped 42% to 997 and are up 20% year-to-date at 1,793. (john.stoll@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 7:37 EST - Abercrombie's (ANF) F4Q revenue fell even more than Wall Street feared, but EPS ended up being right in line with consensus as gross margin rose 1.9 percentage points to 60.9% on lower product costs. And at least inventories seem to be in check, down 13% from a year earlier at quarter-end. Meanwhile, "We expect the first half of 2015 to remain challenging," says Chairman Arthur Martinez between the ongoing sales hit from shrinking its logo business and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  impacts. "However, we believe that the benefits of all of the changes we have made will be reflected in improved performance in the second half of the year." Time will tell. ANF rises 0.7% in initial premarket trading to $24.16 after sliding 3% this week and 16% for 2015. (kevin.kingsbury@wsj.com; @kevinkingsbury)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 March 04, 2015 08:31 ET (13:31 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020150304eb34001u5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
