\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Peru Central Bank \highlight \highlight22\uc2 Intervenes \highlight\uc2 , Sell Dollars -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,286 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Januar 2015\par 20:59\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 14:59 EST - \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was back in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market today, though in a much-smaller way. It sold $5M after a $115M \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  yesterday in efforts to boost the sol, down 7.9% versus the greenback the past year. Despite today's increase in the supply of dollars, it edged up versus the sol to PEN3.045. \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  president Julio Velarde said at a conference "I have the impression that there has been an overreaction in terms of the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate." (robert.kozak@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 14:55 EST - While Yellen's visit to Capitol Hill to speak with \uc2 Senate\uc2  Democrats has garnered plenty of attention today, she wasn't the only Fed official on the Hill today. Coincidentally, \uc2 St. Louis Fed\uc2  chief Bullard was spotted roaming the halls around the same time. He said he was meeting with members from his district and didn't coordinate his visit with Yellen's. The FOMC concluded a 2-day meeting in Washington yesterday. (ben.leubsdorf@wsj.com; @BenLeubsdorf)\par \par \uc2 14:46 EST - Analysts are pretty bad at forecasting \uc2 Boeing\uc2  (BA) cash flow, admits \uc2 Carter Copeland\uc2  at \uc2 Barclays\uc2 , so how much store should investors put in BA delivering higher-than-expected free cash last year and upbeat guidance for 2015? It's the cash metric that's sent the stock soaring in the past two sessions. Copeland says the 2014 cash story could have gone either way, with some items pulled forward from this year, while 2015 guidance lacks any big pension contribution. But with so much churn among industrials as investors avoid emerging market and energy exposure, \uc2 Boeing\uc2  is feeling the love it lacked last year. BA up 5.7% at $147.63. (doug.cameron@wsj.com; @dougcameron)\par \par \uc2 14:40 EST - Yellen's message to \uc2 Senate\uc2  Democrats on the US economy was "very positive," says Minority Whip Richard Durbin after a luncheon with the Fed chairwoman. "She went through the issues of unemployment and inflation. Very positive. And economic-growth numbers were good, have been good." One other bright spot she pointed to was fiscal policy. After restraining growth earlier in the recovery, Yellen said it's now "in a more-neutral position rather than negative," says Durbin. But he notes she also pointed to risks. "We talked about the situation in Europe, one of those risks." (ben.leubsdorf@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 14:31 EST - North Dakota forecasters cut in nearly half their outlook for state revenues from oil-and-gas output, shaving off more than $4B from estimates for the next 2 years. In the face of oil's price collapse, state officials predict the state will collect $4.27B, down from $8.32B in December's forecast, for those 2 years. The state also lowered its outlook this FY and net by $762M to $6.04B. The declines aren't seen hitting general government \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  because North Dakota spends little of its oil-tax revenues on ongoing expenses. (mark.peters@wsj.com; @mrmmpeters)\par \par \uc2 14:28 EST - The Canadian dollar is having a very bad start to 2015, falling 6.6% after dropping 9.8% last year as oil keeps falling. The \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2 's response to oil's implosion--last week's rate cut--added fuel to the fire. It's hard to find anybody who has a good word to say about the loonie; some analysts have penciled in even-lower targets today. Unanimity like that is often seen as an indicator an asset is oversold and maybe due for a rebound. But there are two factors arguing against that: the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market tends to push trends farther than other markets would and it's a cross-asset trade, with oil's tumble the singular, dominant driver of the CAD's decline. Until oil steadies, the loonie won't likely either. (don.curren@wsj.com; @dbcurren)\par \par \uc2 14:27 EST - Sen. Tim Kaine, (D-VA) said Fed Chairwoman \uc2 Janet Yellen\uc2  drew a distinction between the U.S. economy and the rest of the world in her discussion at a luncheon with \uc2 Senate\uc2  Democrats Thursday. "She was generally pretty positive about fundamentals here, you know some concern about the foreign situation. Everyone affects everybody else these days," Mr. Kaine said. (michael.crittenden@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 14:26 EST - As the Canadian dollar continues slide amid oil's weakness (though the commodity has rebounded into the close), the greenback hitting C$1.30 may come into play sooner than many expected. \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  company Knightsbridge had anticipated it happening within 3 months, but it could "easily" get there if oil falls to $40/barrel, says President Rahim Madhavji. He adds C$1.40 is possible if crude slumps to $30. Beyond oil and the potential of another rate cut, there's also policy divergence with the Fed. As \uc2 Nymex\uc2  oil futures earlier breached $44 for first time since 2009, the greenback hit a nearly 6-year high of C$1.2679. "It's a crazy, crazy day today," says Madhavji (nirmala.menon@wsj.com; @NirmalaMenon)\par \par \uc2 14:19 EST - Sen. Joe Manchin, (D-W.V.), said Fed Chairwoman \uc2 Janet Yellen\uc2 's message at a luncheon with \uc2 Senate\uc2  Democrats was straightforward: "Things are going well" for the economy, unemployment is low, but some people are still hurting. "She feels the economy is strong, a lot is good," Mr. Manchin said leaving a lunch with fellow \uc2 Senate\uc2  Democrats Thursday. (michael.crittenden@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 14:12 EST - If they haven't already learned, investors will likely remember in 3 months time to consider whether to own \uc2 Qualcomm\uc2  (QCOM) going into earnings. After July's F3Q report, shares fell 6.7% the next day and 10% in a week's time. After early November's 4Q print, QCOM slumped 8.6% the following day in logging the biggest dollar decline ($6.62) since 2000. Today, it's down $7.78, or 11%, at $63.21 as shares slump to an 18-month low and sit at the bottom of the \uc2 S&P 500\uc2 . \uc2 UBS\uc2  gives up the bull case, downgrading QCOM to neutral and dropping its price target to $64 amid uncertainties in China, peaked market share at \uc2 Samsung\uc2  (005930.SE) and pricing pressure. (kevin.kingsbury@wsj.com; @kevinkingsbury)\par \par \uc2 13:59 EST - It was another strong year for US endowments. At 832 US colleges and universities, the average investing return was 15.5% for the year ended June 30, according to NACUBO-\uc2 Commonfund\uc2  Study of Endowments, versus 11.7% the prior 12 months. When endowments prosper, the additional funds give their schools--many facing state-budget cuts and declining enrollment--a boost to their operating lines. Some 75% of schools grew that type of spending, the study finds. Domestic and international equities, with returns of 23% and 19%, respectively, were the best-performing asset classes in that period. (timothy.martin@wsj.com; @timothywmartin)\par \par \uc2 13:56 EST - Kicking the can down the road doesn't seem to work for many distressed companies. The percentage of repeat defaulters since the Great Recession is 39%, more than double the historical average going back to 1987. That suggests lax credit markets allowed troubled companies to paper over problems without fixing them, according to a new \uc2 Moody's\uc2  report. Many companies which either sought Chapter 11 protection or missed bond payments amid the crisis used the wide-open credit markets to borrow more money or restructure debt. "They were pushing off the inevitable," says \uc2 Moody's\uc2 David Keisman\uc2 . (vipal.monga@wsj.com; @vipalmonga)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 January 29, 2015 14:59 ET (19:59 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020150129eb1t003t1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
