\par\par \b \uc2 Diageo PLC\uc2  Interim Results\b0\par\par\uc2 23,830 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Januar 2015\par 08:01\par \uc2 Regulatory News Service\par \uc2 RNS\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2015   \par \par \uc2 TIDMDGE\par \par \uc2 RNS Number : 4396D\par \par \uc2 Diageo PLC\par \par \uc2 29 January 2015\par \par \uc2 Interim results, six months ended 31 December 2014\par \par \uc2 29 January 2015\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  A strong business improving in a challenging environment \par  \par  \par  \par          *    Organic net sales in the half were broadly flat \par               (-0.1%) with volume down 1.9%. Performance improved \par               in Q2 \par  \par  \par          *    Continued strong performance of reserve brands, up \par               10%, was a key driver of positive overall price/mix \par  \par  \par  \par          *    Marketing spend was in line with net sales, as \par               effective spend benefitted from procurement \par               efficiencies worth 3% of total marketing investment \par  \par  \par          *    Restructuring benefits drove operating margin \par               improvement of 28bps with organic operating profit up \par               0.7% \par  \par  \par          *    Free cash flow was GBP699 million, up GBP373 million \par               on the first half last year \par  \par  \par          *    Eps before exceptional items was 53.7 pence per share, \par               down 8.9 pence per share driven by negative exchange \par               impacts and lower income from associates and joint \par               ventures \par  \par  \par          *    Interim dividend up 9% to 21.5 pence per share \par  \par  \par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 Ivan Menezes\f28 \uc2 \f2 , Chief Executive, commenting on the six months ended 31 \par                              December 2014 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We have improved our performance during the half and we have again shown: the strength of our brands, which is driving our share gains; our strong innovation capability, which has enabled us to access new growth opportunities; and our focus on cost. We delivered the planned savings from our global efficiency programme together with procurement benefits in marketing spend which we have reinvested in our brands and we increased our investment in our routes to consumer while again expanding our margins.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 We have already taken action to improve the performance of those brands and markets that have not performed as well as we would expect. This contributed to our stronger second quarter performance and I expect to maintain this momentum through the year.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The half saw \f28 \uc2 \f2 Diageo\f28 \uc2 \f2  acquire control of USL, putting us in the position to create an iconic leader in spirits in an attractive market. We have also reached agreement to acquire all of Don Julio, which will significantly strengthen our position in one of our fastest growing categories.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The quality of these results in a tough environment, with depletions ahead of shipments and improving cash flow, reinforce my confidence that \f28 \uc2 \f2 Diageo\f28 \uc2 \f2  can realise its full potential and deliver our performance ambition."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Ends\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  movements relating to Venezuela\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 From March 2014 the group has applied the Sicad II rate when consolidating \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in Venezuela. For the six months ended 31 December 2013 the consolidation rate of $1=VEF9 was applied. The change in March 2014 was applied to the total reported \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for the nine months ended 31 March 2014 and subsequent periods. This change reduced the previously reported net sales and operating profit for the six months ended 31 December 2013 by GBP237 million and GBP183 million respectively. This reduction in net sales and operating profit was incorporated into \f28 \uc2 \f2 Diageo\f28 \uc2 \f2 's results for the nine months ended 31 March 2014 and in the Q3 F14 IMS \f28 \uc2 \f2 Diageo\f28 \uc2 \f2  reported net sales decline of 7.4% for the nine months ended 31 March 2014.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Unless otherwise stated, commentary refers to organic movements.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 RESULTS SUMMARY\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Half year results, six months ended 31 December 2014\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Key financial information \par  \par  \par                                                                 First Half  First Half \par Key performance indicators                                             F15         F14 \par --------------------------------------------  --------------   -----------  ---------- \par Organic net sales growth                                    %            -           2 \par ============================================  ===============  ===========  ========== \par Organic operating margin improvement             basis points           28          37 \par ============================================  ===============  ===========  ========== \par Earnings per share before exceptional items             pence         53.7        62.6 \par ============================================  ===============  ===========  ========== \par Free cash flow                                    GBP million          699         326 \par ============================================  ===============  ===========  ========== \par Return on average invested capital                          %         13.9        17.8 \par --------------------------------------------  ---------------  -----------  ---------- \par  \par  \par                                                                          First Half  First Half   Organic   Reported \par                                                    