h as \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates and interest rates. These market inputs are used in the discounted cash flow calculation incorporating the instrument's term, notional amount and discount rate, and taking credit risk into account. As significant inputs to the valuation are observable in active markets, these instruments are categorised as level 2 in the hierarchy.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 There were no significant changes in the measurement and valuation techniques, or significant transfers between the levels of the financial assets and liabilities in the six months ended 31 December 2014.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The group's financial assets and liabilities measured at fair value are categorised as follows:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                                               31 December      30 June  31 December \par                                                      2014         2014         2013 \par                                               GBP million  GBP million  GBP million \par Available-for-sale investments                         72            -            - \par                                               -----------  -----------  ----------- \par Unadjusted quoted prices in active markets \par  (Level 1)                                             72            -            - \par                                               ===========  ===========  =========== \par Derivative assets                                     393          368          405 \par Derivative liabilities                              (215)        (194)        (198) \par                                               -----------  -----------  ----------- \par Valuation techniques based on observable \par  market input (Level 2)                               178          174          207 \par                                               ===========  ===========  =========== \par Other financial liabilities           