\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Peru Central Bank \highlight \highlight22\uc2 Intervenes \highlight\uc2  in  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Market to Sell Dollars -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,311 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 November 2014\par 20:24\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 14:24 EST - \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  today in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, selling $30M to support the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the sol. \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar sales in the last five trading sessions have now reached a total of $625M. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  says it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to ease volatility in the exchange market. The sol has weakened 4.6% against the greenback in the last year. (Robert.kozak@wsj.com @robertkozak2)\par \par \uc2 14:10 EST - NZD/AUD could come under some pressure today if the upcoming October NAB business confidence and conditions survey in Australia shows signs of improvement, says \uc2 ANZ Bank\uc2 . Both confidence and conditions fell in September and "indicators suggest some reversion is probable," it says. NZD/AUD last at 0.8992. \uc2 ANZ Bank\uc2  tips a range of 0.8960 to 0.9060. (rebecca.howard@wsj.com; @FarroHoward)\par \par \uc2 14:01 EST - \uc2 Hellman & Friedman\uc2  is getting by with a little help from its friends. The San Francisco private-equity firm that has backed companies such as \uc2 Nielsen NV\uc2  and \uc2 Getty Images\uc2  wrapped up its latest mega-buyout fund with $10.9B. The firm raised $10.25B -- hitting its so-called "hard cap" -- from institutional investors including pension funds. Another half billion dollars came from the firm itself, with the rest coming from investors whom the firm termed as "friends and family." With the closing, \uc2 Hellman & Friedman\uc2  joins a select group of large-cap firms such as Silver Lake and \uc2 Apollo Global Management\uc2  (APO) that have been able to shrug off lingering uncertainty about the viability of large buyout pools and ended up with more interest than they could accommodate. (hillary.canada@wsj.com; @H_Canada)\par \par \uc2 13:57 EST - Investors traded options at a faster pace in October, pushing contract volume up 22% to 491.4 million from a year earlier, according to research from \uc2 TABB Group\uc2 . That's the second-highest monthly volume on record. Options volume in October was driven by a jump in market volatility, according to TABB research. The \uc2 CBOE\uc2  Volatility Index on Oct. 15 closed at 26.25, the highest level for the year. (saumya.vaishampayan@wsj.com; @saumvaish)\par \par \uc2 13:55 EST - The Colombian peso continued to weaken against the US dollar today amid falling crude oil prices and the slowdown of dollars coming into the economy, hitting 2,095.00, from 2,080.00 a week ago. Analysts at Bancolombia said "we see no turning of the tide," and that the peso will likely reach 2,146.00 in 2015. The fall is good news for exporters, and could help cushion any shock to the economy from lower oil prices, the government's biggest source of export revenues. (sara.munoz@wsj.com; @sarasmunoz)\par \par \uc2 13:53 EST - Farmer's Edge Laboratories is a private company that uses satellite images, computer modeling, soil sampling and weather data to help farmers increase their crop yields and get the most benefit from their land. Offering such products and services puts Farmer's Edge in direct competition with \uc2 Monsanto\uc2  (MON), a multinational agriculture biotechnology company that now offers similar big data and analytics products for farmers. The smaller company has a new ally as it squares off against this much-larger rival, however. Silicon Valley venture firm \uc2 Kleiner Perkins Caufield & Byers\uc2  has invested in the company. (timothy.hay@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 13:52 EST - Airplane Wi-Fi provider GOGO was down some 7% through midday following its 3Q report, but that red is now green in the wake of \uc2 AT&T\uc2  (T) saying it will drop plans to offer a competing service. T disclosing its in-air Wi-Fi intentions in late April sent GOGO shares on a 1-day 29% stock swoon, a decline the company has yet to fully reverse. But with a big potential competitor out of the way and if GOGO can continue to log revenue growth like 3Q's 22%, shares might find an upward trajectory. They're up 1.4% at $16.87, trimming the year's slump to 32%. (kevin.kingsbury@wsj.com; @kevinkingsbury)\par \par \uc2 13:46 EST - ECB executive board member Yves Mersch says Germany's economy didn't do significantly better in 3Q after logging a 0.2% drop in 2Q, saying the Ifo and ZEW surveys "confirm this picture." He is speaking at an event in southwestern Germany sponsored by a local savings bank. Germany's statistics office publishes its first estimate on 3Q GDP Friday; forecasters polled by Dow Jones Newswires expect the German economy to have grown by 0.1%. (todd.buell@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 13:42 EST - A big start for Alibaba's (BABA) financial-services \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the 11/11 shopping event in China known as Singles Day--the country's version of Black Friday or Cyber Monday. Gross merchandise volume settled through the Alipay platform topped $1B within 18 minutes, the company says, with mobile accounting for 48%. And it took an hour and 12 seconds to hit $2B. Prior-year data weren't given. The figures, alas, don't include initial activity done through Alibaba itself, which controls some 80% of China's online-shopping market. But the Alipay numbers do give some insight, notably with mobile. BABA said last week that mobile GMV grew to 36% of the company's total last quarter. BABA rises to session highs on the news and is up 2.5% at $117.40. (kevin.kingsbury@wsj.com; @kevinkingsbury)\par \par \uc2 13:39 EST - \uc2 Teck Resources\uc2  owns 22.5% of Peru's largest copper mine, Antamina, where workers recently launched a strike seeking higher wages. While this disruption shouldn't last more than a few months, says \uc2 BMO\uc2 's \uc2 Aleksandra Bukacheva\uc2 , a year-long strike would slash the projected 2015 global copper surplus by nearly half to 330,000 metric tons. Teck's copper production would shrink 22% 238,000 tons and its zinc output would fall 8%. As a result, Teck's earnings could fall to CAN$0.69/share from a projected CAN$1.16/share, she adds. TCK shares were recently down 2.5% at $16.17 on \uc2 NYSE\uc2 . (tatyana.shumsky@wsj.com; @MissShumsky)\par \par \uc2 13:35 EST - The \uc2 San Francisco Fed\uc2  says in a new paper that the view that changes in the economy point to a lower level of interest rates may be wrong. "Future downward pressure on interest rates may be more muted than indicated by current monetary and fiscal policy projections, which would translate into an upside risk to these longer-term interest rate forecasts," bank economists write. They say economists' forecasts and historical data indicate fears the economy's potential growth rate, and its related level of interest rates, are simply overblown. (michael.derby@wsj.com, @michaelsderby)\par \par \uc2 13:23 EST - \uc2 USDA\uc2 's 2012 move to release market-moving crop reports -- such as today's monthly supply-and-demand estimates -- drew controversy, particularly among old-guard traders who fretted that algorithm-driven firms would get the jump on slower-moving, more fundamental players in the ag markets. Iowa brokerage firm AgriSource today says humans got one over on the machines: Contract prices for wheat, for instance, briefly jumped, but slid after market digested finer points of the lengthy report. "Looks like the High Frequency Traders (HFT) got nailed," AgriSource analysts gloat in a note to clients. (jacob.bunge@wsj.com; @jacobbunge) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par To contact the Market Talk Editors, \par Kevin Kingsbury, 212 416-2354, kevin.kingsbury@wsj.com \par Cynthia Lin, 212 416-4403, Cynthia.lin@wsj.com \par John Shipman, 212 416-2181, john.shipman@wsj.com \par Patrick Sullivan, 212 416-2326, Patrick.sullivan@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 November 10, 2014 14:24 ET (19:24 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020141110eaba003kj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
