\par\par \b \uc2 Peru  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Sells Dollars to Support Sol -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,508 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Oktober 2014\par 22:30\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 16:30 EDT - \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, selling $10M today at PEN2.9051 per US dollar, aiming to support the weakening sol. So far this year the sol has depreciated 3.82% against the greenback, ending today at PEN2.9070. A survey of 21 economic analysts conducted by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  recently found expectations that the sol will end this year at PEN2.90 per dollar. (robert.kozak@wsj.com @robertkozak2)\par \par \uc2 16:27 EDT - Furniture and appliance retailer Conn's (CONN) has been attracting interest from private-equity firms, although no formal inquiries have been made yet, says CEO \uc2 Theodore Wright\uc2 . The Woodlands, Texas-based retailer announced it was exploring strategic alternatives as its stock continues to suffer from its consumer credit portfolio division. "At this point we're evaluating options; it's too early to say whether one alternative is preferred in particular," Wright says. Likely options include selling the company, splitting up its retail and credit divisions, or slowing down on new store openings. "The announcement wasn't related to any financial distress or lack of available capital," Wright adds. CONN down from $44.83 in late August to close at $28.55 today. (lillian.rizzo@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 16:27 EDT - \uc2 Apple\uc2  (AAPL) supplier \uc2 GT Advanced Technologies\uc2  (GTAT) will make its Chapter 11 debut Thursday before Judge Henry J. Boroff in US Bankruptcy Court in Manchester, NH. Boroff, a Massachusetts judge, is stepping in for Judge Bruce A. Harwood, who recused himself. The sapphire screen supplier, which filed for bankruptcy yesterday, has been tight-lipped about its reasons for seeking Chapter 11, saying only in court papers that it was suffering "a severe liquidity crisis due to circumstances that will be more fully described at the hearing." WSJ reported that "liquidity crisis" stems from AAPL withholding a $139M payment. GTAT collapsed 93% Monday following the surprise bankruptcy filing, wiping out roughly $1.4B in market value. Shares bounced 51% to close today at $1.21. (patrick.fitzgerald@wsj.com, @patfitzgerald23)\par \par \uc2 16:21 EDT - \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  (MSFT) CEO \uc2 Satya Nadella\uc2  made a personal appeal to the software maker's core business audience during a wide-ranging interview with analysts at the Gartner Symposium IT/xpo Tuesday. "There is no question that we won't exist if we don't serve you well," Mr. Nadella said. "We want to be in tune with... the value we create for customers." \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  over the last several months has made some major changes to better address competition from \uc2 Amazon.com\uc2 , \uc2 Google\uc2  and others in the mobile and cloud technology segments. In March, the company introduced Office productivity software for \uc2 Apple\uc2  devices. In July, the company said that it would cut 18,000 jobs and make \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  for agile. (clint.boulton@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 16:16 EDT - Telecom companies could face an even louder wakeup call as a growing Internet gets too big for some outdated equipment. Some carriers suffered Web outages in August after a blip briefly puffed up the size of the Internet's map of routes, and network research by Dyn suggests the worry isn't over yet. The Internet is set to grow again beyond the so-called 512K route threshold that stresses older gear in mid-November, Dyn researcher Jim Cowie tells an audience at NANOG, the quarterly conference for network engineers. A research note last month from \uc2 Wells Fargo\uc2  suggested the threat could spur a small but noticeable uptick in spending on certain network gear. (andrew.fitzgerald@wsj.com; @drewfitzgerald)\par \par \uc2 16:12 EDT - \uc2 Dow\uc2  Industrials 209-point Friday rally proves fleeting as the index coughs up about 290 in the subsequent two sessions. Swirl of data and commentary about weakening global growth -- and perhaps a sense that central bankers have flopped in efforts to fuel a sustainable vigorous pickup -- sends equities tumbling. Crude oil hits its lowest settlement since April 22, 2013, and heating oil -- on the precipice of heating season, no less -- sees its lowest settle since June 2012. Ten-year \uc2 Treasury\uc2  yield reaches 4th lowest this year. Not convincing signs of a burgeoning economy. DJIA falls 272.58 to 16719.33, and \uc2 Nasdaq\uc2  Comp loses 69.60 to 4385.20. S&P 500 ends 29.72 lower at 1935.10. (john.shipman@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 16:02 EDT - Companies shipped 8.3B barrels of oil on US pipelines in 2013, up 11% from a year ago, according to federal data compiled by two industry associations and published today. The surging volume of crude shipments outpaced construction of new pipelines, which increased 6% in 2013 from the previous year, according to the \uc2 Association of Oil Pipe Lines\uc2  and the \uc2 American Petroleum Institute\uc2 . The data highlight how drillers are tapping oil from shale-rock formations faster than companies can build new pipelines, even as railroads are taking on a much bigger role in carrying crude. (daniel.gilbert@wsj.com; @WSJGilbert)\par \par \uc2 15:44 EDT - DJIA looks to be headed for its third 200-point-plus move in five sessions (two down, one up), and its 10th triple-digit move in the past 16 sessions. The last time the \uc2 Dow\uc2  moved at least 200 points in three out of five sessions was in late November 2011 (also two down, one up) when Europe's debt crisis was really cooking. Top central bankers then unleashed a "coordinated" action that sent stocks ripping higher, with the \uc2 Dow\uc2  roaring up 490 points on Nov 30, 2011, culminating a three-gain rally that tacked on more than 800 points. (john.shipman@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 15:31 EDT - Overnight strength in AUD and JPY saw the respective NZD crosses push toward the bottom end of recent ranges. NZD/AUD is at 0.8895, close to the 2014 low of 0.8860. BNZ \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Raiko Shareef says if Thursday's jobs data out of Australia is robust, the pair may see a short-term break to 0.8800. He expects the pair at 0.8900 by year-end. NZD/JPY is at 84.66, close to the 84.50 level which proved "fairly robust" early in the year. He doesn't expect a sustainable break below 84.00 in the near-term. (rebecca.howard@wsj.com; @FarroHoward)\par \par \uc2 15:27 EDT - Sen. Charles Schumer (D., N.Y.) says the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  is preparing to implement tougher Ebola screening requirements at US airports this week. Following a call with the health agency's director, Schumer says the measures will go beyond steps announced by the Obama administration yesterday and may reflect recommendations the senator outlined in a letter to the \uc2 CDC\uc2  earlier this month. Schumer had called for active screening -- including taking temperatures -- and creation of a passenger database to be shared with hospitals for passengers arriving from Ebola hotspots in Africa. "The \uc2 CDC\uc2  has been doing a very good job thus far in combating the threat, but you can't be too careful when it comes to stopping a deadly epidemic," Schumer says. (jeffrey.sparshott@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 15:16 EDT - An apparent denial by Interacciones (GFINTERO.MX) CEO \uc2 Carlos Hank Gonzalez\uc2  that his family's niche financial institution is poised to merge with Mexican bank Banorte (GFNORTEO.MX) should relieve share-price pressure of the latter, says brokerage Ve por Mas. Shares are down 9% within the past month amid local press reports about a potential combination. GFINTERO.MX said today that Hank is resigning to join GFNORTEO.MX's board, but it's said the decision isn't due to an agreement to merge the firms. GFNORTEO.MX is down 0.8% today and GFINTERO.MX falls 0.9%; that stock has surged 82% this year. (amy.guthrie@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 15:09 EDT - \uc2 New York Fed\uc2  chief \uc2 William Dudley\uc2  says the market's view that the \uc2 Fed\uc2  will hold off on rate hikes until mid-2015 looks reasonable. "It still is premature to begin to raise interest rates--the labor market still has too much slack and the inflation rate is too low," he says, adding that policy moves will depend on how data evolve. While he welcomes the current path the economy is on, he sees little risk of an upside surprise, and adds that inflation will likely remain below the \uc2 Fed\uc2 's 2% target by 2015-end. Dudley's remarks are a reminder that as much as the heat in the \uc2 Fed\uc2  debate centers around raising rate sooner than expected, core officials are still reluctant to end their de facto zero-bound interest-rate stance. (michael.derby@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par To contact the Market Talk Editors, \par Kevin Kingsbury, 212 416-2354, kevin.kingsbury@wsj.com \par Cynthia Lin, 212 416-4403, Cynthia.lin@wsj.com \par John Shipman, 212 416-2181, john.shipman@wsj.com \par Patrick Sullivan, 212 416-2326, Patrick.sullivan@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 October 07, 2014 16:30 ET (20:30 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020141007eaa7003al\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
