tions, expect the dollar to weaken, the trader says. Volume is heavy. Traders forecast the USD/PHP to stay within 45.00-45.50 in the near term. (cris.larano@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1000 GMT [Dow Jones] Spain's 2.10% April 2017-dated government bond, with its 140 basis ponts pickup against the April 2017-dated German Bobl, remains "very attractive" for carry strategies, according to \uc2 Natixis\uc2 . Spain will auction a total of EUR 4.5 billion to EUR 5.5 billion of the 2.10% April 2017 and the 2.75% April 2019-dated bonds at its next bond sale on Thursday. \uc2 Natixis\uc2  adds that the April 2019-dated Spanish bond appears "relatively cheap" - even against the Italian March 2019 BTP. (emese.bartha@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 February 04, 2014 08:24 ET (13:24 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140204ea24001oz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
