\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Peru \highlight\uc2 's  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight \highlight22\uc2 Intervenes \highlight\uc2  To Support the Sol\b0\par\par\uc2 By Robert Kozak   \par \uc2 204 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 November 2013\par 20:55\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA, \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 --The \uc2 Central Reserve Bank of Peru\uc2  on Monday sold $40 million in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in a bid to ease downward pressures on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the sol--which has weakened 9.76% against the U.S. dollar so far this year.\par \par \uc2 The sol ended trade unchanged Monday at PEN2.801 per U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 Banco de Credito, Peru's largest bank, said in a report late Friday that weakness in the sol is dampening enthusiasm from foreign investors who have bought Peruvian financial instruments as part of a carry-trade strategy.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  actively manages the sol, which alongside the U.S. dollar is legal tender and widely used in Peru.\par \par \uc2 Between 2012 and 2013, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $19.07 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while selling $4.01 billion.\par \par \uc2 A survey carried out by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of economists and companies at the end of October indicated the sol was expected to end the year at PEN2.78 or PEN2.79 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 Write to Robert Kozak at robert.kozak@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 November 11, 2013 14:55 ET (19:55 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020131111e9bb002n4\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\